WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.442
Welcome to CareConsent.

00:00:02.442 --> 00:00:07.323
This updated course follows everyday
hospital work, from patient registration

00:00:07.323 --> 00:00:11.466
and consent choices through remote
withdrawal, assisted reception and

00:00:11.466 --> 00:00:14.288
hospital privacy operations.

00:00:14.288 --> 00:00:18.823
The November edition adds website
preferences, metadata discovery,

00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:23.847
processing records, impact assessments,
vendor review, scoped integrations and

00:00:23.847 --> 00:00:25.871
controlled access.

00:00:25.871 --> 00:00:30.061
We use an invented training hospital and
people throughout.

00:00:30.061 --> 00:00:34.514
Follow the chapters for your role, pause
to practise, and consult the dated

00:00:34.514 --> 00:00:37.335
References and Scope companion.

00:00:37.335 --> 00:00:42.669
Its edition manifest identifies the exact
recorded application build.

00:00:42.669 --> 00:00:47.497
The short animated introduction is
separate from this detailed course.

00:00:48.225 --> 00:00:54.055
Before entering anything, look for Public
synthetic demo or the development warning.

00:00:54.055 --> 00:00:58.794
These screens are for practice, not real
patient registration.

00:00:58.794 --> 00:01:04.305
All names, hospital numbers and contact
references shown here are invented.

00:01:04.305 --> 00:01:09.746
The SMS simulator displays a test code and
sends no text message.

00:01:09.746 --> 00:01:14.472
A green success message in training does
not establish a production deployment,

00:01:14.472 --> 00:01:18.845
legal approval or communication with
another organisation.

00:01:19.558 --> 00:01:24.888
This course uses the reference review
dated fourth November twenty twenty-six.

00:01:24.888 --> 00:01:28.960
Its companion identifies the twenty
twenty-three Digital Personal Data

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:34.222
Protection Act, final twenty twenty-five
Rules, commencement notification, December

00:01:34.222 --> 00:01:37.912
corrigendum and October twenty twenty-six
Order.

00:01:37.912 --> 00:01:42.948
Commencement is phased; not every duty is
already effective.

00:01:42.948 --> 00:01:47.853
Reporting timelines depend on the
applicable provisions and incident.

00:01:47.853 --> 00:01:52.091
A demo retention setting is not a blanket
hospital rule.

00:01:52.091 --> 00:01:57.618
Confirm current applicability and hospital
approval before operational reliance.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.669
Different accounts see different
navigation.

00:02:01.669 --> 00:02:06.478
Reception and clinicians work within
assigned patient scope; privacy officers

00:02:06.478 --> 00:02:11.228
manage privacy cases; auditors inspect
permitted evidence.

00:02:11.228 --> 00:02:15.740
An administrator session has no direct
patient-read permission.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:20.930
However, directory managers can provision
privacy-officer accounts and reset staff

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:25.371
credentials, so they remain trusted
identity operators.

00:02:25.371 --> 00:02:29.490
Stronger privileged appointment and
recovery approval is still an open

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.264
production gate.

00:02:31.264 --> 00:02:36.478
Use your own account, verify hospital and
branch, and never borrow another role to

00:02:36.478 --> 00:02:38.690
bypass a restriction.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:45.068
CareConsent records choices about personal
information for specific purposes.

00:02:45.068 --> 00:02:50.520
It also has a separate register for
references to clinical procedure evidence.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.353
Neither registration, an OTP nor a
downloaded data receipt signs a surgery

00:02:55.353 --> 00:02:57.020
consent form.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:02.163
Clinicians must still complete their
approved procedure-specific process.

00:03:02.163 --> 00:03:07.461
A patient's refusal of optional hospital
offers must not be treated as refusal of

00:03:07.461 --> 00:03:11.669
care or authority to ignore emergency
procedures.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:17.389
At Welcome back, choose CareConsent
Training Hospital in Hospital.

00:03:17.389 --> 00:03:22.246
Enter the Work email and Password provided
for your training role, then select Open

00:03:22.246 --> 00:03:23.806
workspace.

00:03:23.806 --> 00:03:26.853
Read any error before trying again.

00:03:26.853 --> 00:03:30.984
A patient uses a separately provisioned
patient account.

00:03:30.984 --> 00:03:36.008
A consent verification code from reception
is not a workspace password and cannot be

00:03:36.008 --> 00:03:39.124
used to open somebody's patient portal.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:44.278
If an Authenticator code is requested,
obtain the current code from your own

00:03:44.278 --> 00:03:47.692
authenticator app and choose Confirm code.

00:03:47.692 --> 00:03:53.633
For initial enrolment, follow Set up an
authenticator and Confirm authenticator.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:59.323
Inside Readiness & settings, Two-step
sign-in also offers Set up authenticator.

00:03:59.323 --> 00:04:03.061
Save recovery codes privately when they
appear.

00:04:03.061 --> 00:04:07.942
Training screenshots must never be used as
genuine authenticator keys or recovery

00:04:07.942 --> 00:04:09.342
material.

00:04:10.058 --> 00:04:14.665
If the authenticator device is
unavailable, use one unused recovery code

00:04:14.665 --> 00:04:16.829
at the sign-in challenge.

00:04:16.829 --> 00:04:21.496
Stop guessing after failures and contact
the hospital through its official support

00:04:21.496 --> 00:04:22.734
route.

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:28.091
Staff account administration and patient
recovery are different processes.

00:04:28.091 --> 00:04:33.329
Verified patient password recovery
preserves an enabled authenticator.

00:04:33.329 --> 00:04:37.817
If both the patient authenticator and
recovery codes are lost, the dedicated

00:04:37.817 --> 00:04:43.865
Lost authenticator recovery workflow needs
two privacy officers and fresh enrolment.

00:04:43.865 --> 00:04:49.317
This course demonstrates those paths
later; a phone number or consent OTP is

00:04:49.317 --> 00:04:51.790
never a recovery shortcut.

00:04:52.517 --> 00:04:57.002
Open Readiness and settings and find Your
workspace preferences.

00:04:57.002 --> 00:05:01.847
Language offers English plus the
twenty-two Eighth Schedule languages.

00:05:01.847 --> 00:05:07.359
Additional interface catalogs remain
drafts with explicit English fallback.

00:05:07.359 --> 00:05:12.312
English, Tamil, Telugu and Hindi are the
current patient PDF and legal-notice

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:17.371
qualification boundary, not automatically
approved translations.

00:05:17.371 --> 00:05:22.395
Appearance offers System, Light and Dark;
Text size and High contrast support

00:05:22.395 --> 00:05:24.312
comfortable reading.

00:05:24.312 --> 00:05:29.264
These preferences do not translate an old
receipt or change the patient's recorded

00:05:29.264 --> 00:05:31.154
notice language.

00:05:31.892 --> 00:05:36.722
Review patient choices shows the exact
recorded notice language.

00:05:36.722 --> 00:05:41.258
Where an approved recording is available,
Listen to reviewed recording verifies it

00:05:41.258 --> 00:05:44.675
against the published notice before
playback.

00:05:44.675 --> 00:05:49.592
Read using on-device voice is a separately
labelled optional alternative that needs a

00:05:49.592 --> 00:05:51.782
matching installed voice.

00:05:51.782 --> 00:05:55.770
Pause, Resume and Stop reading control
playback.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:06:00.163
If neither route is available, use the
transcript and approved communication

00:06:00.163 --> 00:06:01.699
assistance.

00:06:01.699 --> 00:06:06.746
Playback never establishes agreement,
identity or understanding, and patient

00:06:06.746 --> 00:06:09.664
identifiers are not read aloud.

00:06:10.392 --> 00:06:15.889
Keyboard users can move with Tab and
activate controls with Enter or Space.

00:06:15.889 --> 00:06:18.806
Use Skip to workspace when offered.

00:06:18.806 --> 00:06:23.092
On smaller screens, Open navigation
reveals the menu.

00:06:23.092 --> 00:06:26.592
Increase text size before struggling to
read.

00:06:26.592 --> 00:06:30.365
Offer communication support chosen by the
patient.

00:06:30.365 --> 00:06:35.211
Disability alone does not remove the
person's ability to decide, and an audio

00:06:35.211 --> 00:06:40.364
button does not establish that every
accessibility need has been met.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.466
Select Overview to open Consent overview.

00:06:44.466 --> 00:06:48.680
Registered patients counts records in your
permitted scope.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:53.585
Patients with consent means at least one
active purpose, not permission for every

00:06:53.585 --> 00:06:54.990
purpose.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:59.657
Awaiting consent indicates no recorded
consent in that summary.

00:06:59.657 --> 00:07:03.919
Withdrawn purposes counts individual
purpose withdrawals.

00:07:03.919 --> 00:07:08.442
Read the explanatory labels before
comparing numbers, and remember that your

00:07:08.442 --> 00:07:11.817
role and branch influence what you can
see.

00:07:12.517 --> 00:07:17.502
Look at Needs your attention for privacy
requests and integration work.

00:07:17.502 --> 00:07:22.895
A service target is a date for follow-up,
not proof that a response was sent.

00:07:22.895 --> 00:07:27.169
Pending integration events need
investigation even when local consent was

00:07:27.169 --> 00:07:28.443
saved.

00:07:28.443 --> 00:07:32.502
Use View all patients to continue with the
directory.

00:07:32.502 --> 00:07:37.133
Follow the hospital's escalation process
for overdue requests rather than simply

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:39.969
closing them to clear the dashboard.

00:07:40.683 --> 00:07:44.668
Open Patient directory and select Register
patient.

00:07:44.668 --> 00:07:49.061
Enter Training Adult Patient under Full
name and use a unique training Hospital

00:07:49.061 --> 00:07:50.383
number.

00:07:50.383 --> 00:07:54.871
Enter the agreed synthetic date of birth
and select Department.

00:07:54.871 --> 00:08:00.978
Record the actual contact arrangement:
personal phone, shared phone or no phone.

00:08:00.978 --> 00:08:05.597
Use the agreed synthetic ten-digit number
only when that arrangement includes a

00:08:05.597 --> 00:08:09.490
phone, and record message permission
accurately.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:15.575
Investigate duplicate hospital numbers;
never invent a number to satisfy the form.

00:08:16.308 --> 00:08:20.450
Set Patient notice language to the
language the patient understands,

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:23.662
independently of your interface
preference.

00:08:23.662 --> 00:08:28.031
For this adult exercise, leave guardian
details unused.

00:08:28.031 --> 00:08:32.710
Review every field, then select Save and
review choices.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:37.698
Wait for the saved record or the next
screen before assuming success.

00:08:37.698 --> 00:08:42.305
If validation identifies a mistake,
correct that field.

00:08:42.305 --> 00:08:46.519
Do not invent a guardian or another
person's phone number just to complete

00:08:46.519 --> 00:08:48.177
registration.

00:08:48.892 --> 00:08:53.842
The Review patient choices screen shows
the notice version and language.

00:08:53.842 --> 00:08:58.592
Read Privacy notice and the hospital's
published contact and request channels

00:08:58.592 --> 00:09:00.211
where present.

00:09:00.211 --> 00:09:04.068
In training, a draft warning may remain
visible.

00:09:04.068 --> 00:09:08.865
In real operation, staff must use the
approved effective publication for that

00:09:08.865 --> 00:09:10.318
language.

00:09:10.318 --> 00:09:15.496
An unavailable notice is a stop condition
for this consent workflow, not a reason to

00:09:15.496 --> 00:09:18.121
silently switch languages.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:23.719
Under Choose each purpose separately,
explain each purpose's Data and Use

00:09:23.719 --> 00:09:25.359
descriptions.

00:09:25.359 --> 00:09:30.776
Insurance claim processing does not
automatically approve every recipient.

00:09:30.776 --> 00:09:36.252
Research contact means contact about a
study, not study participation or release

00:09:36.252 --> 00:09:38.347
of research records.

00:09:38.347 --> 00:09:41.430
Hospital news and offers is optional.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:46.157
Select only the patient's agreed purposes,
then ask them to make the displayed

00:09:46.157 --> 00:09:47.800
confirmation.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.959
Do not preselect choices for speed.

00:09:51.683 --> 00:09:56.299
If the patient does not agree, choose
Close without consent.

00:09:56.299 --> 00:09:59.692
No new purpose is granted through this
action.

00:09:59.692 --> 00:10:05.133
Importantly, leaving a box unticked does
not withdraw a purpose granted previously;

00:10:05.133 --> 00:10:08.371
use the separate Withdraw action for that.

00:10:08.371 --> 00:10:12.275
This screen is not a complete
refusal-of-treatment process or an

00:10:12.275 --> 00:10:14.609
emergency decision tool.

00:10:14.609 --> 00:10:18.394
Escalate care questions through the
hospital's approved clinical and

00:10:18.394 --> 00:10:20.840
lawful-basis procedures.

00:10:21.558 --> 00:10:27.662
After the patient confirms the selected
purposes, choose Generate simulated OTP.

00:10:27.662 --> 00:10:33.841
The next screen says SMS simulator — no
message sent and displays Test code.

00:10:33.841 --> 00:10:40.365
Enter that six-digit code in Verification
code, then select Verify & record consent.

00:10:40.365 --> 00:10:45.281
In a qualified live setup, the button and
delivery process differ.

00:10:45.281 --> 00:10:50.043
Never tell a patient that a training test
code arrived by SMS.

00:10:50.767 --> 00:10:54.169
Read any verification error carefully.

00:10:54.169 --> 00:10:59.097
Codes expire after five minutes and allow
a limited number of attempts.

00:10:59.097 --> 00:11:03.657
For an incorrect training code, correct
the entry instead of repeatedly submitting

00:11:03.657 --> 00:11:05.026
guesses.

00:11:05.026 --> 00:11:09.871
Use Change choices if the selected
purposes need changing, then obtain a new

00:11:09.871 --> 00:11:11.276
challenge.

00:11:11.276 --> 00:11:16.002
A code for an earlier notice or different
purposes must not be reused for the new

00:11:16.002 --> 00:11:17.307
choice.

00:11:18.017 --> 00:11:22.990
A network timeout may happen after a
server has accepted an operation.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:27.574
If the screen offers Retry the same
operation, keep the same request intact

00:11:27.574 --> 00:11:30.217
and use that recovery action.

00:11:30.217 --> 00:11:34.300
Avoid double-clicking, changing the form
and treating a retry as a new

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.955
registration.

00:11:35.955 --> 00:11:41.276
Refresh the authorised patient view to
reconcile the result when instructed.

00:11:41.276 --> 00:11:46.062
If the outcome remains unclear, contact
support before recording contradictory

00:11:46.062 --> 00:11:47.509
choices.

00:11:48.225 --> 00:11:53.105
After verification, return to Patient
consent profile and find Signed consent

00:11:53.105 --> 00:11:54.532
receipts.

00:11:54.532 --> 00:12:00.139
Choose Download patient receipt (PDF) for
the relevant purpose and event.

00:12:00.139 --> 00:12:04.567
A grant, a change and a withdrawal can
have different receipts.

00:12:04.567 --> 00:12:08.853
Check that you selected the correct row
before handing over a copy.

00:12:08.853 --> 00:12:13.782
Store downloaded documents securely;
authorised access to a download is not

00:12:13.782 --> 00:12:17.045
permission to leave it on a shared
desktop.

00:12:17.767 --> 00:12:23.005
The PDF shows Your recorded choice,
Purpose, Recorded on, notice information

00:12:23.005 --> 00:12:25.193
and a receipt reference.

00:12:25.193 --> 00:12:29.252
Patient name is labelled as the current
hospital record.

00:12:29.252 --> 00:12:32.931
The notice language belongs to the
recorded event.

00:12:32.931 --> 00:12:38.038
Read Check the latest status: a historical
grant does not guarantee that permission

00:12:38.038 --> 00:12:39.788
is active now.

00:12:39.788 --> 00:12:44.943
The QR opens a status check; the printable
summary is not itself a newly signed

00:12:44.943 --> 00:12:47.116
clinical consent form.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:53.516
Technical verification details contains
Download verification data (JSON) and Copy

00:12:53.516 --> 00:12:56.133
signed token for audit tools.

00:12:56.133 --> 00:13:01.323
Export consent data (JSON) is a separate
profile export containing personal

00:13:01.323 --> 00:13:02.966
information.

00:13:02.966 --> 00:13:08.038
For a public check, open Check a receipt,
paste the signed token or use Scan QR

00:13:08.038 --> 00:13:10.823
image, then choose Check receipt.

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:15.680
Valid signature describes cryptographic
verification; also read withdrawal,

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:20.655
superseded and key-status information
before interpreting the result.

00:13:21.392 --> 00:13:25.832
For staff-assisted withdrawal, open
Patient consent profile and locate the

00:13:25.832 --> 00:13:29.222
granted purpose the patient wants to
withdraw.

00:13:29.222 --> 00:13:31.663
Select its Withdraw button.

00:13:31.663 --> 00:13:36.972
Verify the displayed patient and purpose,
record Patient identity verification or

00:13:36.972 --> 00:13:42.342
request reference under the approved
procedure, and select Confirm withdrawal.

00:13:42.342 --> 00:13:47.115
This is selective: withdrawing insurance
permission does not withdraw every other

00:13:47.115 --> 00:13:48.496
purpose.

00:13:48.496 --> 00:13:53.127
Patients with existing verified accounts
can also withdraw remotely themselves,

00:13:53.127 --> 00:13:58.496
without coming to hospital or supplying a
new consent OTP; the patient chapter shows

00:13:58.496 --> 00:14:00.004
that route.

00:14:00.725 --> 00:14:04.820
Wait for the withdrawal confirmation, then
check that the intended purpose is

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:08.996
Withdrawn while unrelated choices remain
as expected.

00:14:08.996 --> 00:14:13.246
A new withdrawal receipt should appear in
the receipt history.

00:14:13.246 --> 00:14:17.686
The message also explains that downstream
enforcement and legal retention need

00:14:17.686 --> 00:14:18.948
review.

00:14:18.948 --> 00:14:23.901
Do not promise that a laboratory, insurer
or other system has stopped processing

00:14:23.901 --> 00:14:27.745
just because the local status changed
successfully.

00:14:28.475 --> 00:14:32.246
Select Patient directory or Consent
register.

00:14:32.246 --> 00:14:36.865
Use Find patient by name or hospital
number, enter the training name or

00:14:36.865 --> 00:14:39.889
hospital number, then choose Search.

00:14:39.889 --> 00:14:43.365
Previous and Next move through result
pages.

00:14:43.365 --> 00:14:47.508
Open the matching patient only after
checking identity.

00:14:47.508 --> 00:14:52.734
In Patient consent profile, review the
masked contact, notice language, purpose

00:14:52.734 --> 00:14:54.865
statuses and history.

00:14:54.865 --> 00:14:59.335
Similar names are not enough to establish
the correct patient.

00:15:00.058 --> 00:15:05.105
An account may be unable to find or open a
patient because the record is outside its

00:15:05.105 --> 00:15:08.138
hospital, branch or assignment.

00:15:08.138 --> 00:15:12.758
Treat that denial as an access boundary,
not a browser fault.

00:15:12.758 --> 00:15:17.317
Patient linking and staff assignments
require hospital-controlled provisioning;

00:15:17.317 --> 00:15:21.246
this interface has no general Assign
patient button.

00:15:21.246 --> 00:15:24.936
Ask the authorised team to review the
relationship.

00:15:24.936 --> 00:15:28.615
Never ask another person to share their
session.

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:33.300
Open Data sharing and choose Record
sharing approval.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:36.323
Find and select the correct patient.

00:15:36.323 --> 00:15:41.038
Enter Recipient organisation, choose
Purpose and Minimum data category, and

00:15:41.038 --> 00:15:44.978
record Recipient-specific patient approval
evidence.

00:15:44.978 --> 00:15:49.407
Review the expiry explanation, then use
Save record.

00:15:49.407 --> 00:15:54.335
This register records an approval; it does
not transmit reports.

00:15:54.335 --> 00:15:58.859
A general registration OTP does not
authorise disclosure to whichever

00:15:58.859 --> 00:16:02.155
recipient happens to request the
information.

00:16:02.892 --> 00:16:07.689
A clinician with the appropriate patient
scope opens Procedure records and chooses

00:16:07.689 --> 00:16:10.175
Record procedure evidence.

00:16:10.175 --> 00:16:15.139
Select the patient, enter Procedure and
Responsible clinician, then add the Signed

00:16:15.139 --> 00:16:18.865
clinical consent and witness evidence
reference.

00:16:18.865 --> 00:16:22.758
Use Save record after reviewing the source
document.

00:16:22.758 --> 00:16:25.496
This action stores a reference.

00:16:25.496 --> 00:16:30.544
It does not create a patient signature,
witness signature or clinically adequate

00:16:30.544 --> 00:16:33.369
consent document on its own.

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:38.954
For a child, check the date of birth and
the Guardian for consent section.

00:16:38.954 --> 00:16:42.478
Use Add verified guardian when
appropriate.

00:16:42.478 --> 00:16:47.454
Record the guardian's identity, date of
birth, relationship and mobile number,

00:16:47.454 --> 00:16:52.692
then choose How identity was verified and
enter Verification reference.

00:16:52.692 --> 00:16:56.954
Confirm the in-person authority
attestation only after the hospital's

00:16:56.954 --> 00:16:59.014
checks are complete.

00:16:59.014 --> 00:17:02.560
Never enter a full Aadhaar number as the
reference.

00:17:03.267 --> 00:17:07.814
The active guardian panel identifies who
is giving consent and which contact

00:17:07.814 --> 00:17:09.633
receives the code.

00:17:09.633 --> 00:17:13.419
Review these details before generating a
challenge.

00:17:13.419 --> 00:17:18.264
The child's purpose options may be
restricted, including marketing.

00:17:18.264 --> 00:17:23.359
Do not bypass those restrictions or assume
the software applies every healthcare

00:17:23.359 --> 00:17:25.800
exemption automatically.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:30.371
When the child reaches adulthood, guardian
authority and patient access need the

00:17:30.371 --> 00:17:34.752
hospital's approved handover and
identity-review process.

00:17:35.475 --> 00:17:40.296
For an adult, record a lawful guardian
only where verified legal authority

00:17:40.296 --> 00:17:44.663
applies; disability by itself is not
sufficient.

00:17:44.663 --> 00:17:49.758
The form offers appropriate court-order or
guardianship evidence methods.

00:17:49.758 --> 00:17:53.853
Replace guardian starts a new verified
relationship.

00:17:53.853 --> 00:17:58.901
Revoke guardian requires a reason and
affects future consent collection.

00:17:58.901 --> 00:18:03.377
It does not silently cancel every consent
already given.

00:18:03.377 --> 00:18:09.047
Review the guardian history after either
action and escalate uncertain authority.

00:18:09.767 --> 00:18:14.147
A verified patient activates a
hospital-controlled account, chooses a

00:18:14.147 --> 00:18:19.728
private password, then signs in with the
hospital and patient account ID.

00:18:19.728 --> 00:18:24.514
The portal opens Your privacy choices and
Your hospital-linked record.

00:18:24.514 --> 00:18:29.228
Check the identity before continuing; this
is not a phone-number search or open

00:18:29.228 --> 00:18:31.478
self-enrolment service.

00:18:31.478 --> 00:18:35.228
Activation does not itself sign the person
in.

00:18:35.228 --> 00:18:40.288
The later access chapter demonstrates
private handover, activation, recovery and

00:18:40.288 --> 00:18:44.707
the difference between a consent OTP and
an account credential.

00:18:45.433 --> 00:18:49.656
Under Your data requests, choose Send a
data request.

00:18:49.656 --> 00:18:55.918
Request type offers Access, Correction,
Erasure review, Grievance and Nomination.

00:18:55.918 --> 00:19:00.775
Select the appropriate type, explain What
would you like the hospital to do, then

00:19:00.775 --> 00:19:02.883
choose Send request.

00:19:02.883 --> 00:19:07.013
Use a separate, clear request for a
different issue.

00:19:07.013 --> 00:19:12.240
Submission sends work to the privacy team;
it does not immediately correct a record,

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:16.102
erase clinical information or approve a
nominee.

00:19:16.808 --> 00:19:21.534
Choose Read request and response to
inspect the hospital's recorded status and

00:19:21.534 --> 00:19:23.388
response target.

00:19:23.388 --> 00:19:26.769
Refresh my records retrieves updates.

00:19:26.769 --> 00:19:31.234
To withdraw an active permission, choose
Withdraw, check Withdraw this permission

00:19:31.234 --> 00:19:34.031
and confirm with Withdraw permission.

00:19:34.031 --> 00:19:40.115
An existing verified patient account needs
no hospital visit, new consent OTP, reason

00:19:40.115 --> 00:19:43.246
field or staff approval for this action.

00:19:43.246 --> 00:19:46.877
Review Action in connected systems
afterwards.

00:19:46.877 --> 00:19:51.079
Local withdrawal, delivery
acknowledgement, receiver statements and

00:19:51.079 --> 00:19:55.493
independent enforcement verification
remain different facts.

00:19:56.225 --> 00:20:00.460
Staff can receive requests outside the
patient portal.

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:03.794
In Patient rights, choose New request.

00:20:03.794 --> 00:20:08.294
Search for and select the verified
patient, choose Request type and enter

00:20:08.294 --> 00:20:10.175
Request details.

00:20:10.175 --> 00:20:15.448
Record Identity verification / request
reference, then Save record.

00:20:15.448 --> 00:20:19.008
The same five request types are available.

00:20:19.008 --> 00:20:23.389
Reception may record the intake, but
privacy-team permission is required to

00:20:23.389 --> 00:20:26.557
fulfil it or make a retention decision.

00:20:27.267 --> 00:20:32.526
Open Patient rights, locate the Access
case and choose Review request.

00:20:32.526 --> 00:20:37.347
Read Request history, identity evidence
and the service target.

00:20:37.347 --> 00:20:41.907
Download data summary creates a protected
export for the authorised response

00:20:41.907 --> 00:20:43.395
process.

00:20:43.395 --> 00:20:49.109
In Fulfil request, enter How the summary
was provided and any Internal notes.

00:20:49.109 --> 00:20:54.717
Select Fulfil request only after providing
the response through the approved channel.

00:20:54.717 --> 00:20:58.252
Reopen the request to review the saved
result.

00:20:58.252 --> 00:21:02.399
A downloaded file alone is not evidence of
delivery.

00:21:03.100 --> 00:21:07.885
For a Correction case, open the request
and verify the requested change against

00:21:07.885 --> 00:21:09.895
hospital evidence.

00:21:09.895 --> 00:21:14.609
Under Corrected values, complete only the
fields that should change; leave the

00:21:14.609 --> 00:21:16.359
others blank.

00:21:16.359 --> 00:21:21.680
Review the proposed name, contact, date of
birth or language carefully, then use

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:23.597
Fulfil request.

00:21:23.597 --> 00:21:28.466
If more evidence is needed, use Update
status and Awaiting information instead of

00:21:28.466 --> 00:21:29.811
guessing.

00:21:29.811 --> 00:21:33.000
Review the request history after saving.

00:21:33.725 --> 00:21:38.379
Open the Erasure review request and read
the existing patient state and Legal

00:21:38.379 --> 00:21:39.675
holds.

00:21:39.675 --> 00:21:45.032
Under Decision, choose Erase personal data
or Refuse with legal basis only after

00:21:45.032 --> 00:21:48.175
reviewing the applicable records policy.

00:21:48.175 --> 00:21:51.591
If refusing, record the Legal basis.

00:21:51.591 --> 00:21:54.936
Use Fulfil request to apply the decision.

00:21:54.936 --> 00:21:59.341
The system may schedule anonymisation
after required retention instead of

00:21:59.341 --> 00:22:04.250
deleting immediately, and downstream
obligations remain separate.

00:22:04.975 --> 00:22:09.520
In an authorised rights-request detail,
find Legal holds.

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:14.496
Record Reason and Legal basis, then use
Place legal hold when preservation is

00:22:14.496 --> 00:22:16.032
justified.

00:22:16.032 --> 00:22:20.829
To release an active hold, select Release
hold and use the visible release form to

00:22:20.829 --> 00:22:23.460
record the accountable reason.

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:27.663
Confirm the action and verify that the
hold is released, including when the

00:22:27.663 --> 00:22:30.317
request is already completed.

00:22:30.317 --> 00:22:33.234
Cancelling the form releases nothing.

00:22:33.234 --> 00:22:38.234
A released hold does not itself authorise
erasing every record; recheck the

00:22:38.234 --> 00:22:41.067
retention and request decisions.

00:22:41.808 --> 00:22:46.153
Open the Grievance case, read the
patient's concern and check the published

00:22:46.153 --> 00:22:48.019
response target.

00:22:48.019 --> 00:22:52.888
In Fulfil request, enter Response,
retention decision and fulfilment evidence

00:22:52.888 --> 00:22:57.412
with a clear explanation of what was
investigated and decided.

00:22:57.412 --> 00:23:02.269
If the issue is still being investigated,
Update status can record In review or

00:23:02.269 --> 00:23:04.305
Awaiting information.

00:23:04.305 --> 00:23:08.865
Do not label an unresolved complaint
complete just to meet an internal

00:23:08.865 --> 00:23:10.820
dashboard target.

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:16.236
For Nomination, verify the patient's
instructions and complete Nominee name,

00:23:16.236 --> 00:23:22.138
Relationship, Nominee mobile number and
Identity verification / request reference.

00:23:22.138 --> 00:23:25.841
Use Fulfil request after the required
checks.

00:23:25.841 --> 00:23:29.436
The nominee appears in Nominees with a
status.

00:23:29.436 --> 00:23:33.400
Revoke nomination asks for identity
evidence.

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:38.615
Naming a nominee does not give that person
an unrestricted staff account or automatic

00:23:38.615 --> 00:23:42.323
access to the patient's entire hospital
record.

00:23:43.058 --> 00:23:46.936
Select Incident response, then Log an
incident.

00:23:46.936 --> 00:23:52.603
Enter Incident title, the actual time the
hospital became aware, and Nature, scope,

00:23:52.603 --> 00:23:55.412
likely impact and containment.

00:23:55.412 --> 00:23:59.258
Check the computer's timezone before
entering time.

00:23:59.258 --> 00:24:04.900
After saving, open Breach workflow and
complete Assessment: nature, extent,

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:10.996
timing, location, impact, consequences,
mitigation and safety measures.

00:24:10.996 --> 00:24:13.305
Choose Save assessment.

00:24:13.305 --> 00:24:18.310
Do not substitute the time you opened this
screen for earlier awareness.

00:24:19.017 --> 00:24:23.778
Review Initial intimation to the Board and
use Preview message before Send initial

00:24:23.778 --> 00:24:25.324
intimation.

00:24:25.324 --> 00:24:30.526
In this training workspace, the notifier
logs a simulated message; it does not

00:24:30.526 --> 00:24:32.395
contact the Board.

00:24:32.395 --> 00:24:37.728
Add the Hospital numbers of affected
patients using Add affected patients.

00:24:37.728 --> 00:24:43.038
Review the affected list and patient
notice preview before Notify patients.

00:24:43.038 --> 00:24:47.312
Failed or unreachable notices need
follow-up, not an assumption that

00:24:47.312 --> 00:24:49.374
everybody was told.

00:24:50.100 --> 00:24:54.647
Open Detailed report to the Board and
complete the updated description, relevant

00:24:54.647 --> 00:24:58.883
facts, mitigation, findings and remedial
measures.

00:24:58.883 --> 00:25:03.216
Check the assessment and patient-notice
information before choosing Send detailed

00:25:03.216 --> 00:25:05.526
report and confirming.

00:25:05.526 --> 00:25:09.395
This training action records a simulated
report.

00:25:09.395 --> 00:25:14.204
The seventy-two-hour deadline concerns the
detailed report; initial intimation is

00:25:14.204 --> 00:25:15.883
without delay.

00:25:15.883 --> 00:25:21.032
CERT-In reporting is a separate process,
not completed by this screen.

00:25:21.767 --> 00:25:26.862
Before closing a report, Board extension
can record an extension already granted in

00:25:26.862 --> 00:25:28.252
writing.

00:25:28.252 --> 00:25:33.145
Enter Extended deadline and Board
reference, then Record extension.

00:25:33.145 --> 00:25:38.419
To document communication outside this
app, select Record evidence of intimations

00:25:38.419 --> 00:25:40.764
made outside the system.

00:25:40.764 --> 00:25:44.478
Enter the Board references and
affected-person evidence, then Save

00:25:44.478 --> 00:25:45.836
record.

00:25:45.836 --> 00:25:49.824
Use clearly labelled synthetic references
in training.

00:25:49.824 --> 00:25:54.284
Never invent a regulator approval or a
delivery confirmation.

00:25:55.017 --> 00:26:00.383
In Readiness & settings, find Retention
and erasure and choose Add policy.

00:26:00.383 --> 00:26:06.217
Enter Policy name, Applies to, Retention
period, Notice before erasure and Legal or

00:26:06.217 --> 00:26:08.062
records basis.

00:26:08.062 --> 00:26:11.717
Policy is active controls whether it runs.

00:26:11.717 --> 00:26:15.859
Save policy only after hospital records
review.

00:26:15.859 --> 00:26:20.455
The demo's minimums and inactivity
workflow are not universal medical-record

00:26:20.455 --> 00:26:26.309
retention advice, and statutory holds or
other required retention still apply.

00:26:27.017 --> 00:26:32.967
Review Scheduled erasures, Erasure notices
and Recent runs before using Run now.

00:26:32.967 --> 00:26:39.252
That action can carry out due erasures;
practise only on the synthetic exercise.

00:26:39.252 --> 00:26:44.014
Cancel erasure asks why the schedule
should stop, such as verified patient

00:26:44.014 --> 00:26:45.455
contact.

00:26:45.455 --> 00:26:49.824
A hold or patient-contact change can
affect eligibility.

00:26:49.824 --> 00:26:55.217
After a run, inspect notified, failed,
held and cancelled counts, remembering

00:26:55.217 --> 00:26:58.742
that a logged notice is not handset
delivery.

00:26:59.475 --> 00:27:04.165
A privacy author opens Readiness &
settings, then Notice publication and

00:27:04.165 --> 00:27:06.377
Create notice version.

00:27:06.377 --> 00:27:12.079
Enter Version reference, Patient notice
language, title, hospital privacy contact,

00:27:12.079 --> 00:27:15.270
full text and confirmation statement.

00:27:15.270 --> 00:27:20.829
Complete the withdrawal, rights, grievance
and complaint information URLs.

00:27:20.829 --> 00:27:25.675
Select only the consent purposes being
published and enter their names, data,

00:27:25.675 --> 00:27:27.972
uses and categories.

00:27:27.972 --> 00:27:32.087
Create the version, then expand it and
Submit for review.

00:27:32.808 --> 00:27:36.734
Sign in as a different authorised privacy
reviewer.

00:27:36.734 --> 00:27:41.710
Expand the In review version and read the
complete content, purpose definitions and

00:27:41.710 --> 00:27:43.865
communication channels.

00:27:43.865 --> 00:27:48.258
Enter Legal review reference and Language
and audio review reference; where audio

00:27:48.258 --> 00:27:51.984
metadata exists, review its reference too.

00:27:51.984 --> 00:27:56.638
Tick the independent-review attestation
only after checking the actual evidence,

00:27:56.638 --> 00:27:59.377
then choose Approve reviewed version.

00:27:59.377 --> 00:28:02.780
The author cannot approve their own
document.

00:28:03.517 --> 00:28:08.493
An authorised hospital administrator opens
the Approved notice version and selects

00:28:08.493 --> 00:28:10.121
Publish now.

00:28:10.121 --> 00:28:15.097
Publication is for that exact hospital and
language; its current role does not

00:28:15.097 --> 00:28:17.883
directly read patient records.

00:28:17.883 --> 00:28:23.300
Directory administration remains a
separately trusted identity function.

00:28:23.300 --> 00:28:27.312
Notice changes require another version and
review.

00:28:27.312 --> 00:28:31.990
To retire an effective version, enter
Reason for retirement and select Retire

00:28:31.990 --> 00:28:33.312
version.

00:28:33.312 --> 00:28:37.943
Without a replacement, that language's
consent collection becomes unavailable

00:28:37.943 --> 00:28:41.722
instead of silently reverting to an older
notice.

00:28:42.433 --> 00:28:47.290
Platform administration can use Add
hospital to create a hospital identifier,

00:28:47.290 --> 00:28:50.609
name, short code and first branch.

00:28:50.609 --> 00:28:55.418
A hospital administrator operates within
the selected hospital under Hospitals and

00:28:55.418 --> 00:28:56.835
accounts.

00:28:56.835 --> 00:29:01.359
Add branch accepts a branch identifier and
Branch name.

00:29:01.359 --> 00:29:04.442
Verify the hospital before saving.

00:29:04.442 --> 00:29:08.406
Activate and Deactivate change
availability; they do not remove

00:29:08.406 --> 00:29:13.342
historical records or transfer patient
data to another hospital.

00:29:14.058 --> 00:29:19.260
Under Accounts, Add account creates a
synthetic staff learner with Email, Role,

00:29:19.260 --> 00:29:22.019
Branch and Temporary password.

00:29:22.019 --> 00:29:28.079
Patient accounts use the separate verified
patient-access workflow, not this form.

00:29:28.079 --> 00:29:33.900
Staff controls include role Save, Set
password, Unlock, Reset authenticator,

00:29:33.900 --> 00:29:36.341
Activate and Deactivate.

00:29:36.341 --> 00:29:40.103
Treat these as high-trust identity
operations.

00:29:40.103 --> 00:29:44.329
A directory manager can provision a
privacy officer or reset staff

00:29:44.329 --> 00:29:49.031
credentials, so this build does not
establish strong separation from patient

00:29:49.031 --> 00:29:50.496
authority.

00:29:50.496 --> 00:29:55.838
Follow approved appointment, verification
and access-review procedures.

00:29:56.558 --> 00:30:01.867
Authenticator policy lets an administrator
select a Role, set Require authenticator

00:30:01.867 --> 00:30:03.662
and choose Save.

00:30:03.662 --> 00:30:08.722
Plan enrolment and recovery support before
enforcing a requirement.

00:30:08.722 --> 00:30:13.293
Notice delivery lists queued or attempted
notifications with their provider and

00:30:13.293 --> 00:30:14.698
status.

00:30:14.698 --> 00:30:19.210
A log provider is simulation, not an SMS
receipt.

00:30:19.210 --> 00:30:24.496
Administrative resets and policy changes
belong in the access review; they do not

00:30:24.496 --> 00:30:29.867
establish that the hospital has completed
production identity qualification.

00:30:30.600 --> 00:30:35.014
Receipt signing keys is a separate
administrator control.

00:30:35.014 --> 00:30:38.764
Read the listed key states and Public keys
link.

00:30:38.764 --> 00:30:43.133
Only an approved key operator should use
Rotate signing key.

00:30:43.133 --> 00:30:48.276
Rotation retires the previous key; Revoke
accepts a retired key and requires a

00:30:48.276 --> 00:30:49.621
Reason.

00:30:49.621 --> 00:30:53.335
Revocation changes verification outcomes.

00:30:53.335 --> 00:30:57.835
Practise only in the disposable training
hospital, following the key-management

00:30:57.835 --> 00:31:02.589
runbook, and never treat rotation as a
routine reception task.

00:31:03.308 --> 00:31:07.867
An auditor opens Audit trail to inspect
actions within their authorised hospital

00:31:07.867 --> 00:31:09.138
scope.

00:31:09.138 --> 00:31:13.793
Review Actor, time and record references,
then choose Inspect evidence for the

00:31:13.793 --> 00:31:15.615
relevant event.

00:31:15.615 --> 00:31:19.924
Read what the event actually records
instead of assuming it proves every

00:31:19.924 --> 00:31:21.841
external outcome.

00:31:21.841 --> 00:31:26.400
Auditors do not receive general
patient-directory or edit access merely

00:31:26.400 --> 00:31:29.543
because they can inspect audit evidence.

00:31:29.543 --> 00:31:33.833
Handle exported or displayed evidence as
confidential.

00:31:34.558 --> 00:31:39.900
Choose Verify local chain and read the
result and number of events checked.

00:31:39.900 --> 00:31:45.329
A successful result means the available
local chain is internally consistent.

00:31:45.329 --> 00:31:50.055
It does not independently protect against
every privileged database rewrite or

00:31:50.055 --> 00:31:51.638
missing tail.

00:31:51.638 --> 00:31:55.436
Independent signed checkpoints and
separately controlled storage remain

00:31:55.436 --> 00:31:57.269
production work.

00:31:57.269 --> 00:32:02.258
Preserve evidence and escalate a failed
check; do not delete or recreate records

00:32:02.258 --> 00:32:04.818
to make the result turn green.

00:32:05.558 --> 00:32:10.486
In Readiness & settings, inspect Consent
propagation webhooks, Subscribers and

00:32:10.486 --> 00:32:12.008
Deliveries.

00:32:12.008 --> 00:32:16.579
Delivery status filters pending, delivered
and dead-letter work.

00:32:16.579 --> 00:32:21.829
Approved non-public environments can
expose Add subscriber, Dispatch now and

00:32:21.829 --> 00:32:26.817
Retry; the public synthetic demo disables
outbound webhooks.

00:32:26.817 --> 00:32:31.650
Do not demonstrate a real receiver or
reveal a signing secret.

00:32:31.650 --> 00:32:37.450
Delivered describes transport, not proof
that the recipient stopped using data.

00:32:38.183 --> 00:32:43.647
Delivery operations now provides a visible
Processors and outbox view for transport,

00:32:43.647 --> 00:32:47.775
current or stale receiver statements and
operator review.

00:32:47.775 --> 00:32:52.656
Processor registration, contract binding
and authenticated callback integration

00:32:52.656 --> 00:32:55.454
remain technical responsibilities.

00:32:55.454 --> 00:32:59.573
A receiver-attested result is the
receiver's statement, not independent

00:32:59.573 --> 00:33:02.025
proof that processing stopped.

00:33:02.025 --> 00:33:07.263
An older acknowledgement does not
establish the current withdrawal outcome.

00:33:07.263 --> 00:33:11.680
Use the delivery chapter for visible
reconciliation controls and ask the

00:33:11.680 --> 00:33:16.292
integration owner to resolve actual
downstream enforcement.

00:33:17.017 --> 00:33:22.717
The managed edge feature buffers prepared
staff-assisted withdrawal intents only.

00:33:22.717 --> 00:33:27.526
It needs a qualified local node and an
online, short-lived capability prepared

00:33:27.526 --> 00:33:29.050
beforehand.

00:33:29.050 --> 00:33:35.312
Hospital IT operates its APIs; this GUI
has no offline capture switch.

00:33:35.312 --> 00:33:39.609
A locally buffered intent is not yet a
central withdrawal.

00:33:39.609 --> 00:33:44.276
Stale revisions, revoked access, full
storage or missing tickets require

00:33:44.276 --> 00:33:49.633
reconciliation or the approved downtime
process, never automatic offline grants or

00:33:49.633 --> 00:33:52.149
expired OTP replay.

00:33:52.850 --> 00:33:57.778
A patient may have no private phone, share
a family phone, need communication

00:33:57.778 --> 00:34:01.085
support, or require emergency care.

00:34:01.085 --> 00:34:05.502
The current app records contact
preferences, signed-paper or independently

00:34:05.502 --> 00:34:10.621
witnessed data consent, and separate
emergency processing records.

00:34:10.621 --> 00:34:15.526
Those workflows do not create verified
representative authority or replace

00:34:15.526 --> 00:34:18.061
clinical procedure consent.

00:34:18.061 --> 00:34:23.061
Use hospital-approved evidence and
assistance; do not invent contact details

00:34:23.061 --> 00:34:25.895
or reuse another person's code.

00:34:25.895 --> 00:34:30.050
Emergency care must not wait for OTP
completion.

00:34:30.050 --> 00:34:34.535
The reception chapter demonstrates the
available alternatives.

00:34:35.267 --> 00:34:39.324
Internet loss differs from loss of the
hospital server.

00:34:39.324 --> 00:34:44.228
A healthy local server may remain
available on the LAN, while SMS or cloud

00:34:44.228 --> 00:34:46.026
services fail.

00:34:46.026 --> 00:34:50.836
If the server is unreachable, an ordinary
browser save is not automatically

00:34:50.836 --> 00:34:52.181
buffered.

00:34:52.181 --> 00:34:57.026
Check the displayed error, preserve only
approved references and use the agreed

00:34:57.026 --> 00:34:59.050
downtime procedure.

00:34:59.050 --> 00:35:03.943
Do not repeatedly create records or claim
a save succeeded without a durable

00:35:03.943 --> 00:35:05.696
acknowledgement.

00:35:06.433 --> 00:35:11.873
Before finishing, review overdue requests,
unresolved delivery failures, withdrawn

00:35:11.873 --> 00:35:17.216
purposes needing follow-up and any
scheduled erasures or open incidents.

00:35:17.216 --> 00:35:21.633
Hand over responsibilities and evidence
references through the hospital's approved

00:35:21.633 --> 00:35:22.918
channel.

00:35:22.918 --> 00:35:27.799
Secure patient PDFs and exports, clear
shared-device documents according to

00:35:27.799 --> 00:35:30.644
policy and select Sign out.

00:35:30.644 --> 00:35:34.299
Do not leave an account open for the next
shift.

00:35:34.299 --> 00:35:39.693
Return to the relevant chapter whenever a
workflow or permission is uncertain.

00:35:40.433 --> 00:35:45.706
A privacy officer opens the correct adult
patient profile and expands Patient portal

00:35:45.706 --> 00:35:47.133
access.

00:35:47.133 --> 00:35:52.347
Select Enrol verified adult patient,
choose Identity verification method and

00:35:52.347 --> 00:35:55.585
enter the controlled Verification
reference.

00:35:55.585 --> 00:36:00.954
Complete the displayed attestation only
after the approved identity check.

00:36:00.954 --> 00:36:06.121
A hospital number, mobile number or
consent OTP alone does not establish

00:36:06.121 --> 00:36:08.121
portal identity.

00:36:08.121 --> 00:36:12.644
Issue private activation code creates the
protected account relationship;

00:36:12.644 --> 00:36:17.725
registration or consent collection does
not create it automatically.

00:36:18.433 --> 00:36:23.956
The handover shows Patient account ID, a
masked Activation code, expiry, Patient

00:36:23.956 --> 00:36:27.490
activation page and Patient privacy
portal.

00:36:27.490 --> 00:36:32.561
Reveal a code only privately for its
verified recipient, then use Hide handover

00:36:32.561 --> 00:36:33.978
details.

00:36:33.978 --> 00:36:38.311
The addresses do not contain the code or
patient identity.

00:36:38.311 --> 00:36:42.490
Codes expire after fifteen minutes and are
single-use.

00:36:42.490 --> 00:36:47.204
Do not put one in a receipt QR, public
message, support note or shared

00:36:47.204 --> 00:36:48.799
screenshot.

00:36:48.799 --> 00:36:53.299
Closing the panel discards a delayed
secret response; it is not a secure

00:36:53.299 --> 00:36:55.102
storage method.

00:36:55.808 --> 00:37:01.400
On a signed-out phone, tablet or computer,
open Activate patient access.

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:06.031
Choose the hospital, enter the private
Activation code, choose New password and

00:37:06.031 --> 00:37:10.579
Confirm new password, then select Set
password and activate.

00:37:10.579 --> 00:37:14.031
The patient chooses this password
privately.

00:37:14.031 --> 00:37:18.996
Activation creates no signed-in session:
return to sign in using the hospital,

00:37:18.996 --> 00:37:24.150
Patient account ID and chosen password,
then complete any required authenticator

00:37:24.150 --> 00:37:25.388
step.

00:37:25.388 --> 00:37:30.797
No patient directory or phone-number
lookup appears in the patient workspace.

00:37:31.517 --> 00:37:36.147
An existing verified account can withdraw
from Your privacy choices without a

00:37:36.147 --> 00:37:37.978
hospital visit.

00:37:37.978 --> 00:37:43.109
Find the granted purpose, select Withdraw,
review Withdraw this permission and select

00:37:43.109 --> 00:37:45.038
Withdraw permission.

00:37:45.038 --> 00:37:50.109
No reason, fresh consent OTP or staff
approval is required by this patient

00:37:50.109 --> 00:37:51.431
action.

00:37:51.431 --> 00:37:56.228
Verify that only the selected purpose
becomes Withdrawn and download its patient

00:37:56.228 --> 00:37:57.752
PDF.

00:37:57.752 --> 00:38:01.252
Check Action in connected systems
separately.

00:38:01.252 --> 00:38:06.181
Record the portal and reception channels
in the cross-touchpoint assessment; remote

00:38:06.181 --> 00:38:12.674
availability alone does not qualify every
hospital access or enforcement process.

00:38:13.392 --> 00:38:18.296
For a forgotten patient password, the
privacy officer independently verifies the

00:38:18.296 --> 00:38:23.130
person again and uses Verify identity and
recover access with the required

00:38:23.130 --> 00:38:26.282
verification and request references.

00:38:26.282 --> 00:38:30.770
Existing sessions and earlier activation
codes are invalidated; the patient

00:38:30.770 --> 00:38:34.115
receives a new private activation
handover.

00:38:34.115 --> 00:38:38.187
An already enabled authenticator remains
enabled.

00:38:38.187 --> 00:38:42.865
The public activation page explains
official recovery contacts but does not

00:38:42.865 --> 00:38:47.342
accept identity-document uploads or
phone-only resets.

00:38:47.342 --> 00:38:52.008
Loss of the authenticator and all recovery
codes needs the independently reviewed

00:38:52.008 --> 00:38:54.404
factor-recovery workflow.

00:38:55.142 --> 00:38:59.261
Expand Guardian and limited delegate
portal access and choose Request

00:38:59.261 --> 00:39:01.639
representative access.

00:39:01.639 --> 00:39:06.199
Select Current verified guardian or
Limited adult-patient delegate, check the

00:39:06.199 --> 00:39:11.008
applicable authority and expiry, and
record controlled verification and

00:39:11.008 --> 00:39:13.532
authorisation references.

00:39:13.532 --> 00:39:18.234
The first officer uses their own
authenticator; another officer uses

00:39:18.234 --> 00:39:22.246
Independently approve access after a
separate check.

00:39:22.246 --> 00:39:26.842
No private activation handover is issued
at the request stage.

00:39:26.842 --> 00:39:30.353
A guardian needs the current lawful
relationship.

00:39:30.353 --> 00:39:35.425
A limited delegate may inspect permitted
evidence and submit requests, but cannot

00:39:35.425 --> 00:39:38.051
grant or withdraw consent.

00:39:38.767 --> 00:39:43.695
In Staff access to this patient, inspect
current assignments and use Review staff

00:39:43.695 --> 00:39:45.264
assignment.

00:39:45.264 --> 00:39:50.217
Search Staff email for the intended branch
account, choose Grant or renew expiring

00:39:50.217 --> 00:39:55.038
assignment, set the permitted duration and
controlled access-review reference, and

00:39:55.038 --> 00:39:57.907
enter Your current authenticator code.

00:39:57.907 --> 00:40:02.264
Revoke assignment removes that assignment
when access ends.

00:40:02.264 --> 00:40:06.895
Staff role and patient relationship are
both required: an assignment is not

00:40:06.895 --> 00:40:09.383
consent for a new purpose.

00:40:09.383 --> 00:40:13.919
Review shift changes and expiry rather
than leaving permanent links simply for

00:40:13.919 --> 00:40:15.484
convenience.

00:40:16.183 --> 00:40:20.849
When both a patient authenticator and its
recovery codes are lost, open Lost

00:40:20.849 --> 00:40:23.073
authenticator recovery.

00:40:23.073 --> 00:40:27.204
Verify the account and first
identity-check reference, then choose

00:40:27.204 --> 00:40:30.525
Suspend access and request recovery.

00:40:30.525 --> 00:40:35.228
A different privacy officer checks the
independent evidence and uses Approve as

00:40:35.228 --> 00:40:39.787
independent privacy officer with their own
current authenticator.

00:40:39.787 --> 00:40:44.406
The patient receives a new private
activation handover and must enrol a fresh

00:40:44.406 --> 00:40:47.894
authenticator before normal access
resumes.

00:40:47.894 --> 00:40:52.847
Cancellation or expiry does not silently
restore access.

00:40:52.847 --> 00:40:58.060
Do not route patient recovery through
ordinary staff password controls.

00:40:58.767 --> 00:41:04.302
In the patient profile, expand Contact,
assisted consent and emergency records,

00:41:04.302 --> 00:41:07.288
then Verify contact preferences.

00:41:07.288 --> 00:41:11.847
Select the actual personal, shared or
no-phone arrangement, record message

00:41:11.847 --> 00:41:16.097
permission and make the displayed
attestation after checking the patient or

00:41:16.097 --> 00:41:17.871
lawful guardian.

00:41:17.871 --> 00:41:23.788
Save record refreshes the current revision
and invalidates outdated consent codes.

00:41:23.788 --> 00:41:27.931
A shared phone does not create shared
portal identity.

00:41:27.931 --> 00:41:33.026
Sensitive receipt or breach delivery needs
a permitted personal route; unavailable

00:41:33.026 --> 00:41:37.356
delivery becomes alternate work rather
than a false success.

00:41:38.058 --> 00:41:43.153
Under Assisted data consent, choose Signed
paper data consent, record Evidence

00:41:43.153 --> 00:41:47.915
reference ID and select only the patient's
affirmed purposes after explaining the

00:41:47.915 --> 00:41:49.662
current notice.

00:41:49.662 --> 00:41:52.972
Select Prepare evidence for confirmation.

00:41:52.972 --> 00:41:57.424
Preparation grants nothing and expires
after fifteen minutes.

00:41:57.424 --> 00:42:02.555
Inspect the preserved evidence and
explicit affirmation before confirming.

00:42:02.555 --> 00:42:07.579
Keep the original signed document in
approved hospital custody; this app stores

00:42:07.579 --> 00:42:09.781
its controlled reference.

00:42:09.781 --> 00:42:14.805
Successful confirmation uses the normal
consent history and patient-receipt path

00:42:14.805 --> 00:42:18.230
and identifies the paper method
truthfully.

00:42:18.933 --> 00:42:23.111
Choose Affirmation with an independent
witness only when that approved method

00:42:23.111 --> 00:42:25.871
reflects the actual interaction.

00:42:25.871 --> 00:42:30.406
Prepare the selected purposes and evidence
reference, then have another currently

00:42:30.406 --> 00:42:34.644
authorised staff account check the
original evidence and affirmative choice

00:42:34.644 --> 00:42:36.704
before confirmation.

00:42:36.704 --> 00:42:41.204
The preparer cannot serve as the
independent confirming witness.

00:42:41.204 --> 00:42:46.549
Changes to the patient, authority, notice,
assignment or session can invalidate the

00:42:46.549 --> 00:42:48.097
preparation.

00:42:48.097 --> 00:42:53.525
Start again when required; do not reuse an
expired preparation or attempt to restore

00:42:53.525 --> 00:42:56.442
a withdrawn grant through an old form.

00:42:57.142 --> 00:43:01.939
An assigned clinician opens Emergency
processing record, chooses the necessary

00:43:01.939 --> 00:43:06.808
data scope and emergency basis, records
the start time and Clinical record

00:43:06.808 --> 00:43:11.520
reference ID, and selects Record emergency
processing.

00:43:11.520 --> 00:43:15.961
Keep diagnoses and clinical narrative in
the clinical system.

00:43:15.961 --> 00:43:21.032
The clinician later uses Close clinical
episode, and privacy staff use Record

00:43:21.032 --> 00:43:23.615
privacy review for follow-up.

00:43:23.615 --> 00:43:28.842
This records a distinct emergency
processing basis; it grants no consent,

00:43:28.842 --> 00:43:33.663
research or marketing permission, extra
staff access or clinical procedure

00:43:33.663 --> 00:43:35.154
signature.

00:43:35.892 --> 00:43:40.008
Open Delivery operations and select
Patient notices.

00:43:40.008 --> 00:43:44.734
Filter the state or overdue work, then use
Refresh and return to first page when

00:43:44.734 --> 00:43:47.008
checking current progress.

00:43:47.008 --> 00:43:51.306
Pending and Sending do not establish
provider acceptance.

00:43:51.306 --> 00:43:55.080
Submitted does not establish handset
delivery.

00:43:55.080 --> 00:44:00.639
Delivered is a provider-reported delivery
state, not identity or consent.

00:44:00.639 --> 00:44:04.151
Simulated means no real message was sent.

00:44:04.151 --> 00:44:08.889
Unknown needs approved provider
reconciliation; do not assume failure and

00:44:08.889 --> 00:44:11.151
create duplicate sends.

00:44:11.151 --> 00:44:16.281
Use Review this item to record an
evidence-based review or escalation.

00:44:17.017 --> 00:44:22.183
Processors and outbox separates transport
from application acknowledgement and shows

00:44:22.183 --> 00:44:26.526
whether a receiver statement matches the
current consent revision.

00:44:26.526 --> 00:44:31.467
Review this item opens Record delivery
action for a controlled reconciliation or

00:44:31.467 --> 00:44:33.562
escalation reference.

00:44:33.562 --> 00:44:38.455
These actions record a review; they do not
poll the receiver, change consent or

00:44:38.455 --> 00:44:41.502
independently verify enforcement.

00:44:41.502 --> 00:44:46.383
Retry only an eligible explicit rejection
through its available control and the

00:44:46.383 --> 00:44:49.062
approved integration procedure.

00:44:49.062 --> 00:44:54.181
Unknown submission, stale attestations and
missing routing need investigation, not a

00:44:54.181 --> 00:44:57.166
new grant or an invented success.

00:44:57.892 --> 00:45:02.749
Select Alternate delivery to inspect tasks
created when the permitted digital route

00:45:02.749 --> 00:45:04.615
was unavailable.

00:45:04.615 --> 00:45:10.080
Follow the approved phone, paper, assisted
or other hospital procedure outside this

00:45:10.080 --> 00:45:12.842
app, retaining its evidence.

00:45:12.842 --> 00:45:16.984
Then use Review this item and Attest
alternate delivery with the controlled

00:45:16.984 --> 00:45:18.401
reference.

00:45:18.401 --> 00:45:23.080
Cancel an inapplicable task only with an
accountable decision.

00:45:23.080 --> 00:45:28.413
The completed task means a privacy officer
recorded an attestation; it neither grants

00:45:28.413 --> 00:45:33.377
consent nor proves SMS delivery or
downstream enforcement.

00:45:33.377 --> 00:45:37.801
Keep unresolved and overdue work visible
for the next shift.

00:45:38.517 --> 00:45:44.205
Branch synchronization and reconciliation
is a controlled metadata workflow.

00:45:44.205 --> 00:45:48.812
Choose the operational node and use Pull
metadata batch, inspect the offered

00:45:48.812 --> 00:45:54.550
sequence range, then Acknowledge exact
metadata receipt only for that batch.

00:45:54.550 --> 00:46:00.217
A stale historical observation must not
replace the current canonical consent.

00:46:00.217 --> 00:46:05.133
Record an offline intention for review
when reconciliation is required; Close

00:46:05.133 --> 00:46:10.181
review closes the case only and does not
grant or withdraw consent.

00:46:10.181 --> 00:46:15.407
This screen does not supply a full patient
replica, autonomous multi-writer consent

00:46:15.407 --> 00:46:18.426
or universal offline registration.

00:46:19.142 --> 00:46:24.094
Managed node identity lets an authorised
operator verify and bind the managed

00:46:24.094 --> 00:46:28.844
machine's public key and approved origin
using current node state, a controlled

00:46:28.844 --> 00:46:32.008
reference and their actual authenticator.

00:46:32.008 --> 00:46:36.389
Confirm key binding only after checking
the authorised machine operator and

00:46:36.389 --> 00:46:38.449
replacement impact.

00:46:38.449 --> 00:46:42.830
Rotate the node public key and Revoke this
credential are separate controlled

00:46:42.830 --> 00:46:44.306
actions.

00:46:44.306 --> 00:46:49.294
The private key stays on its managed host
and must never enter the form, video or

00:46:49.294 --> 00:46:51.032
support notes.

00:46:51.032 --> 00:46:56.103
Revocation stops that credential receiving
new metadata; it does not erase an

00:46:56.103 --> 00:46:58.091
existing replica.

00:46:58.808 --> 00:47:03.546
Open Production operations readiness to
inspect configuration checks, the signing

00:47:03.546 --> 00:47:07.793
probe, current branch counters and
Operational alerts.

00:47:07.793 --> 00:47:12.222
A synthetic environment should not appear
production-qualified.

00:47:12.222 --> 00:47:16.877
Record operations evidence accepts an
actual artifact reference, its SHA

00:47:16.877 --> 00:47:21.769
two-fifty-six digest, performed time and
operator-reported outcome for activities

00:47:21.769 --> 00:47:27.710
such as restore, key rotation, incident
exercise and security assessment.

00:47:27.710 --> 00:47:31.722
Missing, failed or stale evidence stays
visible.

00:47:31.722 --> 00:47:36.341
Download signed audit anchor preserves a
local checkpoint; the hospital must

00:47:36.341 --> 00:47:41.222
separately qualify protected storage,
monitoring, recovery and independent

00:47:41.222 --> 00:47:42.485
review.

00:47:43.225 --> 00:47:47.605
External checkpoints and alert delivery
displays its enabled or disabled

00:47:47.605 --> 00:47:49.496
deployment state.

00:47:49.496 --> 00:47:53.639
Demonstrations make no external operations
calls.

00:47:53.639 --> 00:47:58.175
In a qualified configuration, Queue
current checkpoint for signing creates an

00:47:58.175 --> 00:48:02.329
immutable snapshot for the controlled
delivery pipeline.

00:48:02.329 --> 00:48:06.996
Retry this export preserves the same
export; acknowledgement is still a

00:48:06.996 --> 00:48:09.020
receiver statement.

00:48:09.020 --> 00:48:13.686
Managed receipt signing uses separately
provisioned versioned keys and does not

00:48:13.686 --> 00:48:17.151
silently fall back during a vault outage.

00:48:17.151 --> 00:48:21.615
Neither the screen nor this course
provisions a vault, immutable archive,

00:48:21.615 --> 00:48:25.174
monitoring destination or on-call service.

00:48:25.892 --> 00:48:30.949
FHIR and HL7 connections is optional and
disabled by default.

00:48:30.949 --> 00:48:36.246
The visible System clients, Purpose codes,
Demographic review and Sync log belong to

00:48:36.246 --> 00:48:41.806
a controlled integration facade, not a
general patient-access entitlement.

00:48:41.806 --> 00:48:46.663
Actual credential provisioning needs an
authorised current privacy officer, real

00:48:46.663 --> 00:48:49.401
authenticator and reviewed scope.

00:48:49.401 --> 00:48:53.996
No production hospital system is connected
in this tutorial.

00:48:53.996 --> 00:48:59.270
Do not interpret terminology in the screen
as SMART Backend Services certification,

00:48:59.270 --> 00:49:03.889
or imported demographics as verified
guardian authority or permission to send

00:49:03.889 --> 00:49:05.369
messages.

00:49:06.100 --> 00:49:10.538
Ayushman Bharat, or ABDM, is also
optional.

00:49:10.538 --> 00:49:14.430
The default screen reports that it is not
enabled.

00:49:14.430 --> 00:49:19.680
This build permits only an explicitly
configured local synthetic mock; it does

00:49:19.680 --> 00:49:23.811
not open NHA sandbox or production
exchange.

00:49:23.811 --> 00:49:29.645
Do not enter real Aadhaar, ABHA or
clinical records in a training exercise.

00:49:29.645 --> 00:49:34.383
No ABHA is required for the app's ordinary
data-consent journey.

00:49:34.383 --> 00:49:39.764
A local artefact, callback or transfer
demonstration does not establish authentic

00:49:39.764 --> 00:49:44.811
national consent verification, provider
authentication or externally qualified

00:49:44.811 --> 00:49:46.729
record exchange.

00:49:47.433 --> 00:49:52.668
Languages and translations shows review
status and language versions.

00:49:52.668 --> 00:49:57.144
The interface offers twenty-three
selectable locales, but drafts and English

00:49:57.144 --> 00:50:00.013
fallback are explicitly labelled.

00:50:00.013 --> 00:50:05.454
Export JSON or Export XLIFF supports the
controlled review process; Import

00:50:05.454 --> 00:50:10.787
translation draft stores a draft and does
not replace a published notice or silently

00:50:10.787 --> 00:50:12.906
update the interface.

00:50:12.906 --> 00:50:18.311
The current legal and PDF qualification
boundary remains English, Tamil, Telugu

00:50:18.311 --> 00:50:21.811
and Hindi with actual approval still
required.

00:50:21.811 --> 00:50:26.894
Reviewed recordings must match the exact
published version and digest; generic

00:50:26.894 --> 00:50:29.358
server speech is disabled.

00:50:30.058 --> 00:50:34.724
Open Privacy workspace with a
privacy-officer account, or inspect it as

00:50:34.724 --> 00:50:36.722
a read-only auditor.

00:50:36.722 --> 00:50:41.043
Twenty framework outcomes and evidence
gaps separates Software workflow from

00:50:41.043 --> 00:50:44.484
Hospital evidence and remaining
qualification.

00:50:44.484 --> 00:50:49.472
Register and review workflow available
means the software exists.

00:50:49.472 --> 00:50:54.496
No evidence registered, Incomplete or
awaiting review, Review overdue and

00:50:54.496 --> 00:50:59.079
Current approved records present describe
the registered evidence, not complete

00:50:59.079 --> 00:51:01.008
hospital coverage.

00:51:01.008 --> 00:51:04.281
Open register moves to the relevant area.

00:51:04.281 --> 00:51:09.353
Start with an agreed scope and actual
owners, not a target of making every card

00:51:09.353 --> 00:51:10.590
green.

00:51:11.308 --> 00:51:16.638
Under Controlled registers, choose the
data inventory register and New record.

00:51:16.638 --> 00:51:21.472
Enter Record title, Responsible owner and
Review due date, then the actual

00:51:21.472 --> 00:51:26.996
collection sources, subject and data
categories, purposes, storage, access,

00:51:26.996 --> 00:51:31.079
sharing and retention information
requested by the form.

00:51:31.079 --> 00:51:37.008
Cover clinical systems, laboratories,
billing, human resources, websites, paper,

00:51:37.008 --> 00:51:41.353
processors and backups through
appropriately scoped records.

00:51:41.353 --> 00:51:46.246
Keep patient details and raw documents out
of these metadata fields.

00:51:46.246 --> 00:51:50.579
Save draft records work; original
controlled evidence remains in its

00:51:50.579 --> 00:51:52.560
governed repository.

00:51:53.267 --> 00:51:57.517
Choose the data-flow register to document
how a source sends information to a

00:51:57.517 --> 00:52:02.505
destination, why the flow exists, which
categories and recipients are involved,

00:52:02.505 --> 00:52:05.919
and the countries or safeguards being
assessed.

00:52:05.919 --> 00:52:09.859
Use the form's controlled references to
connect the assessment to the real

00:52:09.859 --> 00:52:11.871
interface evidence.

00:52:11.871 --> 00:52:17.002
Reconcile the map against the inventory
and responsible system owners.

00:52:17.002 --> 00:52:21.645
Do not assume that a diagram or a saved
assessment creates an integration,

00:52:21.645 --> 00:52:27.127
validates its destination or stops an
unconnected system using information.

00:52:27.850 --> 00:52:32.909
Use the obligations register to document
applicable requirements, the identified

00:52:32.909 --> 00:52:36.859
gap, its priority, action and evidence.

00:52:36.859 --> 00:52:40.966
Then choose the separate governance
register for accountable and responsible

00:52:40.966 --> 00:52:45.335
roles, deputies, escalation and decision
authority.

00:52:45.335 --> 00:52:50.430
These are different records reached
through Register, not one combined form.

00:52:50.430 --> 00:52:56.228
Hospital legal, privacy, IT, operations,
procurement and leadership must validate

00:52:56.228 --> 00:52:58.359
their responsibilities.

00:52:58.359 --> 00:53:03.109
Dates and owner names alone do not
establish that an action happened.

00:53:03.109 --> 00:53:08.335
Keep unresolved gaps explicit and revisit
them at the recorded review date.

00:53:09.058 --> 00:53:13.474
Choose the privacy and cookie policy
register for the actual policy or

00:53:13.474 --> 00:53:19.353
procedure version, its scope, effective
date, owner and controlled evidence.

00:53:19.353 --> 00:53:24.638
Include the full organisational privacy
policy and relevant operating procedures;

00:53:24.638 --> 00:53:28.877
a purpose-specific patient notice is not
the whole policy.

00:53:28.877 --> 00:53:33.079
Keep original documents in approved
custody and record their reference and

00:53:33.079 --> 00:53:35.091
digest for review.

00:53:35.091 --> 00:53:39.448
A material change requires a new reviewed
record revision.

00:53:39.448 --> 00:53:44.138
The hospital must separately approve and
publish the real wording, contacts and

00:53:44.138 --> 00:53:46.375
operating arrangements.

00:53:47.100 --> 00:53:50.933
Choose the tracker and preference
assessment register for each relevant

00:53:50.933 --> 00:53:54.014
hospital website or application.

00:53:54.014 --> 00:53:59.038
Record the identifiers or trackers
present, their purpose and classification,

00:53:59.038 --> 00:54:03.466
and evidence of any required preference or
blocking controls.

00:54:03.466 --> 00:54:08.073
The essential session cookie in this app
is not a reason to invent a blanket cookie

00:54:08.073 --> 00:54:09.347
banner.

00:54:09.347 --> 00:54:14.514
If a conditional area genuinely does not
apply, document a substantive scope and

00:54:14.514 --> 00:54:16.788
applicability rationale.

00:54:16.788 --> 00:54:21.597
Actual hospital sites and third-party
software still need inspection; saving

00:54:21.597 --> 00:54:25.352
this assessment cannot disable an external
tracker.

00:54:26.058 --> 00:54:31.236
Begin with the vendor assessment register
for services, safeguards, subprocessors,

00:54:31.236 --> 00:54:33.424
findings and follow-up.

00:54:33.424 --> 00:54:37.412
Use the separate agreement register for
the reviewed contract version,

00:54:37.412 --> 00:54:41.031
responsibilities and security
arrangements.

00:54:41.031 --> 00:54:46.519
Use the cross-border transfer register for
actual locations, flows, restrictions and

00:54:46.519 --> 00:54:48.115
safeguards.

00:54:48.115 --> 00:54:52.888
Choose each through Register; the example
background is one vendor form, not a

00:54:52.888 --> 00:54:54.805
merged questionnaire.

00:54:54.805 --> 00:55:00.150
Procurement, legal and system owners must
review genuine artifacts and execute any

00:55:00.150 --> 00:55:02.281
required agreements.

00:55:02.281 --> 00:55:07.198
A processor registration or typed contract
reference alone does not complete due

00:55:07.198 --> 00:55:08.678
diligence.

00:55:09.392 --> 00:55:14.642
Use the privacy impact assessment register
for a real activity, technology or

00:55:14.642 --> 00:55:16.437
proposed change.

00:55:16.437 --> 00:55:21.937
Identify the people and data affected, the
privacy risk, planned mitigation, residual

00:55:21.937 --> 00:55:27.627
risk, decision, accountable owner and
review evidence requested by the form.

00:55:27.627 --> 00:55:32.342
Keep risk acceptance explicit and retain
the underlying assessment.

00:55:32.342 --> 00:55:37.258
Do not choose a verified outcome while
mitigation is merely planned.

00:55:37.258 --> 00:55:41.627
The hospital must assess whether
additional legal duties apply; the app

00:55:41.627 --> 00:55:47.692
does not automatically classify every
hospital as a significant data fiduciary.

00:55:48.392 --> 00:55:52.737
The rights-fulfilment register records a
controlled request reference, target

00:55:52.737 --> 00:55:57.842
system, deadline, decision, performed
action and verification.

00:55:57.842 --> 00:56:03.020
The separate retention register records a
category, legal schedule, holds, backup

00:56:03.020 --> 00:56:07.234
treatment and actual disposal or retention
evidence.

00:56:07.234 --> 00:56:11.842
The background here shows the retention
example; switch Register for the rights

00:56:11.842 --> 00:56:13.139
record.

00:56:13.139 --> 00:56:18.199
Existing patient-request screens perform
their supported local actions, but neither

00:56:18.199 --> 00:56:22.984
assessment form edits every clinical
system, deletes a processor's copy or

00:56:22.984 --> 00:56:25.484
proves backup expiry.

00:56:25.484 --> 00:56:29.764
Keep those external actions and
limitations in the evidence.

00:56:30.475 --> 00:56:35.058
Use the children's protection assessment
register to review actual collection,

00:56:35.058 --> 00:56:40.522
purposes, identity and authority checks,
applicable safeguards and any claimed

00:56:40.522 --> 00:56:42.103
exemption.

00:56:42.103 --> 00:56:47.055
The existing guardian workflow and purpose
blocks are controls to assess, not a

00:56:47.055 --> 00:56:50.127
complete organisational conclusion.

00:56:50.127 --> 00:56:54.115
Check connected systems and the transition
to adulthood.

00:56:54.115 --> 00:56:59.246
Healthcare exceptions require a relevant
purpose and applicable conditions; do not

00:56:59.246 --> 00:57:02.996
assume every hospital activity is exempt.

00:57:02.996 --> 00:57:07.841
Disability alone does not remove an
adult's decision-making rights or create

00:57:07.841 --> 00:57:10.287
lawful guardian authority.

00:57:11.017 --> 00:57:15.731
Choose the training register to record the
controlled course, content version, staff

00:57:15.731 --> 00:57:21.181
role or cohort, completion date,
assessment method and exceptions.

00:57:21.181 --> 00:57:26.252
It is a completion-evidence register, not
an automatic learning platform.

00:57:26.252 --> 00:57:30.205
Use the separate continuous-review
register for scheduled assessments,

00:57:30.205 --> 00:57:35.693
regulatory changes, audit findings, risk,
corrective action, owner and closure

00:57:35.693 --> 00:57:37.419
verification.

00:57:37.419 --> 00:57:42.836
The background shows the training example;
change Register for review work.

00:57:42.836 --> 00:57:48.359
Actual employees must learn and
responsible owners must verify closure.

00:57:48.359 --> 00:57:53.589
Future planned training cannot be approved
as already verified completion.

00:57:54.308 --> 00:57:59.793
In a patient profile, Marketing consent
preflight offers Check current consent.

00:57:59.793 --> 00:58:04.650
It checks the current local marketing
purpose, age, erasure or retention state

00:58:04.650 --> 00:58:07.984
and an authorised personal SMS route.

00:58:07.984 --> 00:58:13.400
Care consent and OTP message permission do
not imply marketing permission.

00:58:13.400 --> 00:58:17.758
The preview grants no dispatch permission
and sends nothing.

00:58:17.758 --> 00:58:23.638
In Privacy workspace, separately assess
the real CRM, segmentation, recipients,

00:58:23.638 --> 00:58:27.865
campaign eligibility and cross-touchpoint
withdrawal process.

00:58:27.865 --> 00:58:32.948
The actual sender must enforce suppression
immediately before each send; a stale

00:58:32.948 --> 00:58:35.920
preview cannot authorise a campaign.

00:58:36.642 --> 00:58:41.618
Use the security and operations register
to identify the control, qualified

00:58:41.618 --> 00:58:46.344
environment, acceptance criteria,
performed date, observed result and

00:58:46.344 --> 00:58:48.342
remaining findings.

00:58:48.342 --> 00:58:53.365
Link genuine operations, restore,
monitoring, access-review or assessment

00:58:53.365 --> 00:58:54.830
evidence.

00:58:54.830 --> 00:58:59.722
A planned future test cannot be approved
as verified performance.

00:58:59.722 --> 00:59:04.639
Directory administrators remain trusted
identity roots capable of provisioning or

00:59:04.639 --> 00:59:09.258
resetting privacy-officer accounts;
stronger privileged lifecycle separation

00:59:09.258 --> 00:59:11.972
is still open engineering work.

00:59:11.972 --> 00:59:17.139
Production key custody, protected backups,
real recovery, on-call delivery and

00:59:17.139 --> 00:59:21.662
independent assessment also need actual
commissioning evidence.

00:59:22.392 --> 00:59:25.856
Choose the breach and incident
operational-readiness register for an

00:59:25.856 --> 00:59:29.139
actual exercise or incident scenario.

00:59:29.139 --> 00:59:34.353
Record detection, ownership, applicable
reporting clocks and channels, delivery

00:59:34.353 --> 00:59:39.568
and escalation results, investigation,
containment, recovery and corrective

00:59:39.568 --> 00:59:41.020
actions.

00:59:41.020 --> 00:59:44.913
Link the controlled incident or exercise
evidence.

00:59:44.913 --> 00:59:49.806
This supplements the existing incident
workflow shown earlier; it does not submit

00:59:49.806 --> 00:59:52.687
a report or establish delivery.

00:59:52.687 --> 00:59:58.556
Assess DPDP and CERT-In duties separately
and check their current applicability.

00:59:58.556 --> 01:00:03.401
A tabletop record cannot prove that a real
contact route, response team or

01:00:03.401 --> 01:00:05.972
notification service works.

01:00:06.683 --> 01:00:11.540
For any register, New record opens its
specific required fields together with

01:00:11.540 --> 01:00:15.835
Record title, Responsible owner and Review
due date.

01:00:15.835 --> 01:00:18.978
Enter only bounded governance metadata.

01:00:18.978 --> 01:00:23.918
Use Controlled evidence reference and
Artifact SHA two-fifty-six to identify the

01:00:23.918 --> 01:00:27.430
original artifact kept in its governed
location.

01:00:27.430 --> 01:00:32.418
Save draft can preserve work before that
evidence is ready, but Submit for review

01:00:32.418 --> 01:00:36.573
requires both a controlled reference and
valid digest.

01:00:36.573 --> 01:00:41.454
The app does not upload or authenticate
the original document merely because these

01:00:41.454 --> 01:00:43.280
fields are filled.

01:00:44.017 --> 01:00:48.633
Open View record and inspect its current
revision and Review history.

01:00:48.633 --> 01:00:53.919
Select Submit for review, provide Decision
reason and confirm the submission.

01:00:53.919 --> 01:00:58.455
A different current DPO from both the
creator and last editor must inspect the

01:00:58.455 --> 01:01:00.193
real evidence.

01:01:00.193 --> 01:01:04.586
That officer chooses Approve record
revision or Reject record revision and

01:01:04.586 --> 01:01:08.978
enters their own actual Authenticator code
and decision reason.

01:01:08.978 --> 01:01:12.800
A demo fallback code cannot perform this
review.

01:01:12.800 --> 01:01:17.717
Approval applies only to the submitted
revision; it is not hospital certification

01:01:17.717 --> 01:01:21.286
or proof of independent external
assurance.

01:01:22.017 --> 01:01:26.909
Edit record changes require the observed
revision and reset earlier approval to

01:01:26.909 --> 01:01:28.264
Draft.

01:01:28.264 --> 01:01:33.336
Reopen as draft returns a submitted,
rejected or approved record for a fresh

01:01:33.336 --> 01:01:34.586
review.

01:01:34.586 --> 01:01:39.288
Stale edits fail rather than overwrite
another person's work, and immutable

01:01:39.288 --> 01:01:42.407
Review history preserves prior revisions.

01:01:42.407 --> 01:01:47.764
An approved record that still identifies a
gap remains incomplete evidence; overdue

01:01:47.764 --> 01:01:50.228
review dates remain visible.

01:01:50.228 --> 01:01:55.764
If the result is unknown, use Retry same
operation with the unchanged intent.

01:01:55.764 --> 01:02:00.836
Refresh records also retries a failed
initial catalog load; do not create

01:02:00.836 --> 01:02:03.797
duplicates to work around an error.

01:02:04.517 --> 01:02:09.731
Download evidence JSON exports the
bounded, consistent branch snapshot and

01:02:09.731 --> 01:02:11.478
record history.

01:02:11.478 --> 01:02:15.836
Download readable report creates a
printable evidence and gap report with

01:02:15.836 --> 01:02:21.074
owners, review dates, references, findings
and remaining gates.

01:02:21.074 --> 01:02:25.574
Original documents are not embedded, and
the report is not a signed compliance

01:02:25.574 --> 01:02:27.145
certificate.

01:02:27.145 --> 01:02:31.443
Use the evidence-pack register to
reconcile the complete organisational

01:02:31.443 --> 01:02:35.764
scope and accountable final decision
across branches.

01:02:35.764 --> 01:02:41.395
Oversized exports fail explicitly instead
of silently omitting records.

01:02:41.395 --> 01:02:46.609
Before real-patient release, close genuine
implementation, integration, hospital

01:02:46.609 --> 01:02:52.322
approval and independent-assessment gaps;
completing the course does not close them.

01:02:53.058 --> 01:02:58.093
The November update requires authenticator
enrolment for staff outside demo mode

01:02:58.093 --> 01:03:00.829
before a full session is issued.

01:03:00.829 --> 01:03:05.186
A shared hospital network has separate
account and address rate budgets, and

01:03:05.186 --> 01:03:08.627
repeated wrong passwords still lock an
account.

01:03:08.627 --> 01:03:13.305
These production controls differ from the
password-only synthetic demo shown in

01:03:13.305 --> 01:03:15.234
earlier chapters.

01:03:15.234 --> 01:03:19.948
Train staff in authenticator enrolment and
protected recovery.

01:03:19.948 --> 01:03:25.222
Directory administrators remain trusted
identity operators; a separate approval

01:03:25.222 --> 01:03:29.558
for every privileged appointment has not
been demonstrated.

01:03:30.267 --> 01:03:35.481
Open the intended patient profile, then
Contact, assisted consent and emergency

01:03:35.481 --> 01:03:36.919
records.

01:03:36.919 --> 01:03:42.526
Verify the intended phone or private email
address under the hospital procedure.

01:03:42.526 --> 01:03:48.133
Choose SMS, Email or SMS and email in
Preferred delivery channel, record the

01:03:48.133 --> 01:03:52.931
relevant authorisation and contact
attestation, then save.

01:03:52.931 --> 01:03:55.728
The address shown here is invented.

01:03:55.728 --> 01:04:00.026
Guardian contact forms have the
corresponding channel fields.

01:04:00.026 --> 01:04:05.086
Production delivery still requires an
approved provider and templates.

01:04:05.086 --> 01:04:09.919
Contract and sandbox routes remain
explicitly non-production, and an Android

01:04:09.919 --> 01:04:15.167
gateway is a development pilot option
rather than production qualification.

01:04:15.892 --> 01:04:21.032
Deployment uses a separate migrate command
before starting the API.

01:04:21.032 --> 01:04:26.092
The owner migration connection must be
removed from the runtime environment.

01:04:26.092 --> 01:04:30.913
Production startup checks validate the
configured policy, distinct secrets,

01:04:30.913 --> 01:04:35.199
secure transport and protected application
key storage.

01:04:35.199 --> 01:04:38.889
The November corrections address the
reviewed migration command and

01:04:38.889 --> 01:04:44.663
key-protection wiring; consult the dated
qualification record for actual results.

01:04:44.663 --> 01:04:49.151
Rehearse the intended Production profile
instead of treating a development smoke

01:04:49.151 --> 01:04:51.651
test as deployment proof.

01:04:51.651 --> 01:04:56.365
Hospital notices, processor agreements,
operational ownership and independent

01:04:56.365 --> 01:04:59.161
assessment remain separate gates.

01:04:59.892 --> 01:05:04.722
In Settings, open Notice publication and
create a new version.

01:05:04.722 --> 01:05:09.675
For each selected purpose, describe the
information and its use, then choose the

01:05:09.675 --> 01:05:11.984
approved lawful basis.

01:05:11.984 --> 01:05:15.996
A consent purpose remains a separate
optional choice.

01:05:15.996 --> 01:05:21.199
For a qualifying section seven purpose,
enter the exact lawful-use notice text as

01:05:21.199 --> 01:05:22.365
well.

01:05:22.365 --> 01:05:27.211
The emergency example here is invented and
must not be copied as a general

01:05:27.211 --> 01:05:29.139
routine-care basis.

01:05:29.139 --> 01:05:33.853
Submit the version for a different
reviewer and an authorised publisher.

01:05:33.853 --> 01:05:39.921
A saved draft does not become the patient
notice until that lifecycle is complete.

01:05:40.642 --> 01:05:45.199
In the patient profile, expand Lawful use
and child health.

01:05:45.199 --> 01:05:49.984
Review the exact published purpose and its
stated lawful basis.

01:05:49.984 --> 01:05:54.913
When the approved procedure applies,
explain that notice, confirm that it was

01:05:54.913 --> 01:05:58.568
shown, and choose Record lawful-use
notice.

01:05:58.568 --> 01:06:04.472
The saved history records this separate
event; it does not create a consent grant.

01:06:04.472 --> 01:06:10.115
In the consent journey, only consent-based
purposes are selectable checkboxes.

01:06:10.115 --> 01:06:15.222
The illustrated medical emergency is a
narrow training example, not a claim that

01:06:15.222 --> 01:06:19.662
all routine care is an emergency or a
permission for marketing.

01:06:20.392 --> 01:06:26.199
An authorised privacy officer opens
Hospital privacy policy in Settings.

01:06:26.199 --> 01:06:30.639
Keep the child healthcare exemption
disabled until the hospital has approved

01:06:30.639 --> 01:06:33.437
the decision and its narrow scope.

01:06:33.437 --> 01:06:38.103
If it applies, record the legal review
reference and decision, select only the

01:06:38.103 --> 01:06:42.092
approved care or telemedicine purposes,
and save.

01:06:42.092 --> 01:06:45.984
Marketing, research and insurance are
excluded.

01:06:45.984 --> 01:06:50.211
The panel also sets the maximum
limited-delegate count.

01:06:50.211 --> 01:06:54.734
Saving these controls is not legal
approval, and a limited delegate still

01:06:54.734 --> 01:06:57.637
cannot grant or withdraw consent.

01:06:58.350 --> 01:07:02.600
With the reviewed policy configured,
return to the intended child patient

01:07:02.600 --> 01:07:06.371
profile and expand Lawful use and child
health.

01:07:06.371 --> 01:07:11.359
In Child healthcare exemption, select only
the approved health purpose and enter the

01:07:11.359 --> 01:07:15.085
actual reason and controlled clinical
reference.

01:07:15.085 --> 01:07:19.597
Choose Record child health exemption and
inspect the history.

01:07:19.597 --> 01:07:24.597
This records the scoped exception; it does
not grant optional consent or give new

01:07:24.597 --> 01:07:26.454
staff access.

01:07:26.454 --> 01:07:31.526
A qualifying exception must not become a
general guardian bypass.

01:07:31.526 --> 01:07:36.842
Keep verified guardian procedures for the
circumstances that require them.

01:07:37.558 --> 01:07:43.353
Verification codes belong to a particular
patient, contact route and request.

01:07:43.353 --> 01:07:48.829
Saving a contact change cancels unused
challenges; begin a new confirmation using

01:07:48.829 --> 01:07:50.591
the correct route.

01:07:50.591 --> 01:07:55.448
Replacing or removing email is a separate
explicit choice so a masked address is

01:07:55.448 --> 01:07:58.888
never accidentally submitted as an
address.

01:07:58.888 --> 01:08:04.246
Before capture, confirm the recipient and
explain the specified purposes.

01:08:04.246 --> 01:08:09.377
A code verifies a step through that route;
it does not establish every aspect of

01:08:09.377 --> 01:08:14.803
identity, agreement to treatment or
agreement to every future use.

01:08:15.517 --> 01:08:21.145
The privacy evidence export now includes
an application HMAC signature.

01:08:21.145 --> 01:08:25.597
It can detect an alteration when checked
with the appropriate protected application

01:08:25.597 --> 01:08:26.800
key.

01:08:26.800 --> 01:08:30.967
It does not independently timestamp the
evidence or prove that a referenced

01:08:30.967 --> 01:08:35.169
contract, deletion or assessment actually
happened.

01:08:35.169 --> 01:08:40.252
Preserve the original export and verify it
through the supported procedure.

01:08:40.252 --> 01:08:45.969
The export still explicitly says that
production approval has not been granted.

01:08:46.683 --> 01:08:50.966
Open the privacy workspace and expand
Review reminders.

01:08:50.966 --> 01:08:54.573
Choose Scan reminders to refresh the work
list.

01:08:54.573 --> 01:08:59.430
Review the record, review window and due
date, then return to the underlying case

01:08:59.430 --> 01:09:02.978
or governance record to complete the
actual work.

01:09:02.978 --> 01:09:07.942
Entries cover applicable seven-day,
one-day and overdue windows; an empty list

01:09:07.942 --> 01:09:12.252
is not a certificate that the entire
hospital has no gaps.

01:09:12.252 --> 01:09:17.811
These are work-list entries, not evidence
that a notification reached its owner.

01:09:17.811 --> 01:09:22.128
Keep an accountable person and retain
completion evidence.

01:09:22.850 --> 01:09:27.407
Open the correct incident and expand
Regulatory filing evidence.

01:09:27.407 --> 01:09:32.264
When the CERT-In duty applies, enter the
real first-awareness time, category and

01:09:32.264 --> 01:09:35.788
responsible contact, then open the clock.

01:09:35.788 --> 01:09:38.800
The screen shows its six-hour deadline.

01:09:38.800 --> 01:09:43.180
Use the filing form to record the
reference and hash of an actual submitted

01:09:43.180 --> 01:09:46.788
report, not merely a notification log.

01:09:46.788 --> 01:09:50.204
The values here are an invented exercise.

01:09:50.204 --> 01:09:53.859
This screen never submits a report to a
regulator.

01:09:53.859 --> 01:09:58.633
Preserve awareness time, escalate promptly
and follow the approved incident

01:09:58.633 --> 01:10:00.142
procedure.

01:10:00.850 --> 01:10:05.635
Board submission evidence is separate from
CERT-In filing and from sending patient

01:10:05.635 --> 01:10:07.442
notifications.

01:10:07.442 --> 01:10:12.073
Choose the initial or detailed stage that
applies, enter the genuine submission

01:10:12.073 --> 01:10:16.157
reference and report hash, and record the
evidence.

01:10:16.157 --> 01:10:18.526
Review the saved history.

01:10:18.526 --> 01:10:24.300
This does not itself send the report or
establish that an authority accepted it.

01:10:24.300 --> 01:10:28.776
The hospital must assess the applicable
legal phase and deadlines, preserve the

01:10:28.776 --> 01:10:33.002
original report in its controlled
repository and retain proof of the actual

01:10:33.002 --> 01:10:34.454
submission.

01:10:34.454 --> 01:10:39.030
Training entries must never be reused as
real filing evidence.

01:10:39.767 --> 01:10:45.052
The public receipt-verification page now
explains its essential security cookie and

01:10:45.052 --> 01:10:48.431
offers a separate optional preference
choice.

01:10:48.431 --> 01:10:52.859
Choose Essential only when optional
storage is unnecessary.

01:10:52.859 --> 01:10:58.574
This website preference is separate from
the patient purposes on a hospital notice.

01:10:58.574 --> 01:11:02.859
It must never be described as clinical
consent or permission to use health

01:11:02.859 --> 01:11:04.276
records.

01:11:04.276 --> 01:11:09.467
Receipt verification checks the evidence
presented; it does not establish a patient

01:11:09.467 --> 01:11:13.556
account or give access to all hospital
information.

01:11:14.267 --> 01:11:18.612
Patients should receive the readable
receipt and retain its identifier when

01:11:18.612 --> 01:11:20.597
contacting support.

01:11:20.597 --> 01:11:25.193
Use the authorised verification route and
avoid posting private receipts or

01:11:25.193 --> 01:11:28.181
identifiers in public messages.

01:11:28.181 --> 01:11:32.847
Public notice wording and translated
interface text still require independent

01:11:32.847 --> 01:11:35.586
review before patient publication.

01:11:35.586 --> 01:11:40.324
A selected language does not establish
approved legal wording.

01:11:40.324 --> 01:11:45.371
Essential website security storage,
optional website preferences and patient

01:11:45.371 --> 01:11:48.439
data purposes are separate decisions.

01:11:49.142 --> 01:11:54.094
Use the dated qualification report to
establish which exact application version

01:11:54.094 --> 01:11:55.972
and checks passed.

01:11:55.972 --> 01:11:59.806
The November corrections include
production startup and key handling,

01:11:59.806 --> 01:12:04.532
incident scope, lawful-purpose filtering,
delivery fields and keyboard access to

01:12:04.532 --> 01:12:06.449
scrolling tables.

01:12:06.449 --> 01:12:11.294
A recording shows the exercised synthetic
journey; build, backend and browser

01:12:11.294 --> 01:12:13.949
results add their own evidence.

01:12:13.949 --> 01:12:18.639
None of these substitutes for an
independent security assessment, an actual

01:12:18.639 --> 01:12:23.163
Production-profile rehearsal, real service
qualification or a restore from the

01:12:23.163 --> 01:12:25.499
intended backup system.

01:12:26.225 --> 01:12:30.248
Rehearse with synthetic people in a
separate non-demo environment using the

01:12:30.248 --> 01:12:33.567
reviewed application and configuration.

01:12:33.567 --> 01:12:39.067
Test first staff authenticator enrolment,
verified reception, approved notices,

01:12:39.067 --> 01:12:43.639
purpose choices, remote patient
withdrawal, restricted-role denials and

01:12:43.639 --> 01:12:46.103
downstream acknowledgements.

01:12:46.103 --> 01:12:51.651
Exercise provider failure, retries, lost
connectivity and restore.

01:12:51.651 --> 01:12:56.603
Record the source version, configuration,
results and owner of every remaining

01:12:56.603 --> 01:12:58.115
exception.

01:12:58.115 --> 01:13:02.960
A successfully recorded demo is useful
training evidence, but it does not turn

01:13:02.960 --> 01:13:06.974
the public synthetic service into a
patient deployment.

01:13:07.683 --> 01:13:12.837
Before real patient use, the hospital
needs approved notices and lawful bases,

01:13:12.837 --> 01:13:17.813
verified guardian and assisted procedures,
qualified delivery and hospital-system

01:13:17.813 --> 01:13:22.409
enforcement, working managed keys and
backups, monitoring ownership and

01:13:22.409 --> 01:13:26.478
independent security and accessibility
acceptance.

01:13:26.478 --> 01:13:30.966
The product supports that programme; it
does not automatically certify the

01:13:30.966 --> 01:13:32.430
hospital.

01:13:32.430 --> 01:13:36.549
Use the training chapters to understand
the workflow, then keep the readiness

01:13:36.549 --> 01:13:40.415
register accurate as the implementation
changes.

01:13:41.142 --> 01:13:45.889
Open Privacy platform and identify the
website you are reviewing.

01:13:45.889 --> 01:13:50.746
Enter its name and exact origin, then
paste a bounded cookie snapshot and scan

01:13:50.746 --> 01:13:51.842
it.

01:13:51.842 --> 01:13:55.258
The inventory groups supplied names for
review.

01:13:55.258 --> 01:13:59.734
A familiar cookie name alone cannot
establish what the script actually does,

01:13:59.734 --> 01:14:03.258
and this action does not crawl every page.

01:14:03.258 --> 01:14:07.949
Inspect the source, purpose and actual
browser behaviour with the website owner

01:14:07.949 --> 01:14:10.865
before relying on the classification.

01:14:10.865 --> 01:14:16.371
Website storage choices remain separate
from patient information purposes.

01:14:17.100 --> 01:14:22.669
The published website preference centre
identifies the hospital and website.

01:14:22.669 --> 01:14:26.085
Essential security storage stays on.

01:14:26.085 --> 01:14:30.728
A visitor can choose optional categories,
save them and later select essential

01:14:30.728 --> 01:14:32.526
cookies only.

01:14:32.526 --> 01:14:38.240
Wait for a genuine acknowledgement; a
failed request must not appear saved.

01:14:38.240 --> 01:14:42.335
The browser remembers choices when storage
is available.

01:14:42.335 --> 01:14:47.073
After withdrawal, reload the website as
instructed and verify the actual

01:14:47.073 --> 01:14:49.157
integrated scripts.

01:14:49.157 --> 01:14:53.907
These choices concern this browser and
website; they do not change a patient

01:14:53.907 --> 01:14:57.249
account or authorise hospital marketing.

01:14:57.975 --> 01:15:02.320
The website integration helper exposes
choice checks and preference-change

01:15:02.320 --> 01:15:03.686
events.

01:15:03.686 --> 01:15:07.365
The website team must connect each
optional script to the appropriate

01:15:07.365 --> 01:15:12.139
category, remove uncontrolled early
loading and test grant and withdrawal in a

01:15:12.139 --> 01:15:13.889
fresh browser.

01:15:13.889 --> 01:15:19.472
Existing third-party scripts may require a
reload and their own disposal steps.

01:15:19.472 --> 01:15:24.055
This chapter explains that integration
boundary; the preference screen is not

01:15:24.055 --> 01:15:28.948
evidence that every tracker on a real
hospital website is blocked.

01:15:28.948 --> 01:15:33.084
Keep a website-specific test record before
release.

01:15:33.808 --> 01:15:37.400
Open Data discovery and processing
records.

01:15:37.400 --> 01:15:40.936
Give the connector a recognisable system
name.

01:15:40.936 --> 01:15:45.817
A contract connector accepts declared
column metadata for review.

01:15:45.817 --> 01:15:50.186
A PostgreSQL connector uses
server-managed, approved connection

01:15:50.186 --> 01:15:55.138
configuration; do not enter database
credentials in this form.

01:15:55.138 --> 01:16:01.793
Record only metadata, never actual patient
names, phone numbers or clinical values.

01:16:01.793 --> 01:16:06.388
The resulting inventory describes what was
supplied or configured, and cannot

01:16:06.388 --> 01:16:10.620
establish that every hospital system has
been discovered.

01:16:11.350 --> 01:16:16.028
Select the connector and supply one line
per declared field, following the visible

01:16:16.028 --> 01:16:21.240
system, table, field, purpose, retention
and country format.

01:16:21.240 --> 01:16:23.883
Inspect the resulting items.

01:16:23.883 --> 01:16:28.823
Record a source-to-destination flow, its
purpose, countries and approved safeguard

01:16:28.823 --> 01:16:30.228
reference.

01:16:30.228 --> 01:16:35.264
This exercise uses invented system names
and no actual transfer.

01:16:35.264 --> 01:16:40.061
Ask the real system owners to confirm the
map and keep it current when interfaces

01:16:40.061 --> 01:16:41.371
change.

01:16:41.371 --> 01:16:46.675
A declared flow does not prove that its
receiving system obeys a withdrawal.

01:16:47.392 --> 01:16:53.044
Generate a record of processing activities
after reviewing the inventory and flows.

01:16:53.044 --> 01:16:57.806
Inspect the activities, date and source
evidence, then download the report if

01:16:57.806 --> 01:16:59.211
required.

01:16:59.211 --> 01:17:03.461
Ask the accountable system owners to
correct omissions.

01:17:03.461 --> 01:17:08.449
A processing record is useful only when it
reflects actual hospital practices,

01:17:08.449 --> 01:17:12.806
including external processors and
retention arrangements.

01:17:12.806 --> 01:17:17.865
Generating a report does not provide legal
approval, and its production-approval flag

01:17:17.865 --> 01:17:20.821
must not be interpreted as granted.

01:17:21.558 --> 01:17:25.805
Generate the gap assessment and inspect
its unmet controls.

01:17:25.805 --> 01:17:31.162
The score summarises recorded inputs and
rules; it does not independently examine

01:17:31.162 --> 01:17:34.258
the hospital or certify compliance.

01:17:34.258 --> 01:17:38.115
Open the full evidence where the summary
is abbreviated.

01:17:38.115 --> 01:17:43.460
Turn each applicable gap into a concrete
owner, due date and verifiable action in

01:17:43.460 --> 01:17:45.543
the hospital programme.

01:17:45.543 --> 01:17:51.267
Keep unverified work open, even if another
part of the dashboard looks green.

01:17:51.975 --> 01:17:56.975
When closing programme work, retain the
controlled reference, reviewer, date and

01:17:56.975 --> 01:17:58.305
result.

01:17:58.305 --> 01:18:03.115
Review summaries may show only a bounded
number of returned records, with full

01:18:03.115 --> 01:18:05.782
evidence available separately.

01:18:05.782 --> 01:18:10.258
Do not mistake an empty table for proof
that there is no work, or a saved

01:18:10.258 --> 01:18:13.686
attestation for independent verification.

01:18:13.686 --> 01:18:18.627
Use the existing governance workspaces to
maintain owners, reviews and acceptance

01:18:18.627 --> 01:18:22.115
evidence alongside these platform reports.

01:18:22.850 --> 01:18:27.633
Create an impact assessment for a specific
processing activity.

01:18:27.633 --> 01:18:32.478
Select the appropriate template, describe
the activity and enter justified

01:18:32.478 --> 01:18:37.264
likelihood, impact and mitigation values,
with a review date.

01:18:37.264 --> 01:18:42.109
The residual score is a structured aid,
not a substitute for examining the real

01:18:42.109 --> 01:18:43.359
risk.

01:18:43.359 --> 01:18:47.347
Submit the assessment with supporting
decision evidence.

01:18:47.347 --> 01:18:51.883
This synthetic example uses invented
processing and is not an approval of a

01:18:51.883 --> 01:18:54.142
real hospital service.

01:18:54.850 --> 01:18:59.300
A different authorised officer reviews the
submitted assessment.

01:18:59.300 --> 01:19:04.050
They inspect the activity, mitigation and
supporting evidence before approving or

01:19:04.050 --> 01:19:05.680
rejecting it.

01:19:05.680 --> 01:19:08.978
The author cannot approve their own
submission.

01:19:08.978 --> 01:19:13.835
Reopen when processing or assumptions
change, rather than silently editing an

01:19:13.835 --> 01:19:15.680
approved result.

01:19:15.680 --> 01:19:20.716
Current record revisions protect this
workflow against stale updates.

01:19:20.716 --> 01:19:25.300
An internal approval is not independent
security testing or permission to start

01:19:25.300 --> 01:19:27.630
every form of processing.

01:19:28.350 --> 01:19:33.169
Register the vendor and its service, then
select it in the questionnaire.

01:19:33.169 --> 01:19:37.192
Tick a control only when reviewed evidence
supports it.

01:19:37.192 --> 01:19:42.038
The computed score reflects those answers;
it is not an independent audit of the

01:19:42.038 --> 01:19:43.514
provider.

01:19:43.514 --> 01:19:49.145
Keep missing controls visible and follow
up through procurement and privacy review.

01:19:49.145 --> 01:19:53.823
This training vendor is fictional and its
selected answers demonstrate the workflow

01:19:53.823 --> 01:19:56.715
rather than endorse any service.

01:19:57.433 --> 01:20:02.159
After the real agreement has been executed
through the approved process, record its

01:20:02.159 --> 01:20:06.811
controlled reference and expiry against
the current vendor revision.

01:20:06.811 --> 01:20:09.037
Check the saved result.

01:20:09.037 --> 01:20:13.597
Entering a reference in CareConsent does
not sign the agreement or verify its

01:20:13.597 --> 01:20:15.609
original artifact.

01:20:15.609 --> 01:20:20.716
Our synthetic reference is explicitly an
exercise, so it must not be used as

01:20:20.716 --> 01:20:23.299
evidence of a real contract.

01:20:23.299 --> 01:20:28.702
Keep procurement ownership and renewal
review outside this demonstration clear.

01:20:29.433 --> 01:20:34.513
Select the patient through the authorised
search and locate declared records.

01:20:34.513 --> 01:20:39.121
Confirm the hospital and branch scope
before inspecting the result.

01:20:39.121 --> 01:20:44.002
Location metadata helps plan a rights
response, but does not retrieve all

01:20:44.002 --> 01:20:48.823
clinical values or establish a complete
cross-system disclosure.

01:20:48.823 --> 01:20:53.204
Continue through the actual rights-request
workflow and contact the responsible

01:20:53.204 --> 01:20:57.582
system owners for information not held by
this application.

01:20:58.308 --> 01:21:03.948
Select the patient and the exact purpose,
then check the current result and reason.

01:21:03.948 --> 01:21:08.996
A permit is current informational evidence
within the authorised scope; a denial must

01:21:08.996 --> 01:21:12.936
not be overridden by reusing an older
response.

01:21:12.936 --> 01:21:18.174
A historical lawful-use notice does not
create blanket present permission.

01:21:18.174 --> 01:21:23.198
The receiving application must re-evaluate
at use time and also enforce its other

01:21:23.198 --> 01:21:25.412
applicable restrictions.

01:21:25.412 --> 01:21:29.385
The result is not a reusable marketing
authorisation.

01:21:30.100 --> 01:21:34.242
Create a named connector only after
approving its purpose and integration

01:21:34.242 --> 01:21:35.788
permissions.

01:21:35.788 --> 01:21:41.323
Select the minimum required purposes and
purpose-check or security-ingest scope.

01:21:41.323 --> 01:21:46.073
Provide your current authenticator and a
controlled evidence reference.

01:21:46.073 --> 01:21:49.514
The server derives the hospital and
branch.

01:21:49.514 --> 01:21:54.716
The credential is displayed privately once
and stays masked in this recording.

01:21:54.716 --> 01:21:59.645
Transfer it directly to the approved
secret store, then clear it.

01:21:59.645 --> 01:22:04.811
It must never appear in a screenshot,
exported evidence, source control or a

01:22:04.811 --> 01:22:06.720
patient receipt.

01:22:07.433 --> 01:22:12.254
Select the current connector, confirm its
identity and revoke it using your current

01:22:12.254 --> 01:22:15.216
authenticator and evidence reference.

01:22:15.216 --> 01:22:18.013
Check that the result is inactive.

01:22:18.013 --> 01:22:22.847
A lost original key response requires
revoke and reissue, rather than retrieving

01:22:22.847 --> 01:22:25.287
a raw secret from history.

01:22:25.287 --> 01:22:30.478
Store rotations and dependent-service
changes in the operational procedure.

01:22:30.478 --> 01:22:35.133
Revoking this connector does not recall
data already delivered or prove that

01:22:35.133 --> 01:22:38.413
another system deleted its own copies.

01:22:39.142 --> 01:22:43.306
Select the patient and approved
privacy-notice template.

01:22:43.306 --> 01:22:47.734
Confirm that the patient specifically
authorised this WhatsApp notice and that

01:22:47.734 --> 01:22:51.163
the intended recipient is private and
correct.

01:22:51.163 --> 01:22:55.496
Record the controlled authorisation
reference before sending.

01:22:55.496 --> 01:23:00.330
SMS permission alone is not WhatsApp
permission, and a shared number needs the

01:23:00.330 --> 01:23:02.687
approved privacy review.

01:23:02.687 --> 01:23:08.151
This exercise uses the local test provider
and invented contact information; it does

01:23:08.151 --> 01:23:11.154
not send a real hospital message.

01:23:11.892 --> 01:23:14.972
Inspect the recorded dispatch result.

01:23:14.972 --> 01:23:20.818
Simulated or submitted means exactly that;
it does not prove delivery.

01:23:20.818 --> 01:23:25.639
A verified provider receipt is a separate
fact, and receiving a notice is not the

01:23:25.639 --> 01:23:28.353
patient’s affirmative consent.

01:23:28.353 --> 01:23:32.889
Resolve failed or unknown delivery through
the reconciliation process without

01:23:32.889 --> 01:23:35.532
inventing a successful result.

01:23:35.532 --> 01:23:40.568
Before live use, the hospital must qualify
the provider, approved templates,

01:23:40.568 --> 01:23:45.561
recipient handling and receipt
verification under its chosen service.

01:23:46.267 --> 01:23:50.969
Describe what happened, the nature of the
incident, likely consequences and

01:23:50.969 --> 01:23:53.050
containment measures.

01:23:53.050 --> 01:23:58.288
Identify the responsible contact and link
the incident where available.

01:23:58.288 --> 01:24:02.681
Record investigation findings from
evidence, without overstating what is

01:24:02.681 --> 01:24:03.895
known.

01:24:03.895 --> 01:24:09.109
Build the pack and inspect its contents
before sharing through an approved route.

01:24:09.109 --> 01:24:13.752
This exercise contains invented facts and
is not an actual breach report or

01:24:13.752 --> 01:24:15.759
regulator submission.

01:24:16.475 --> 01:24:22.282
Use the saved pack identifier to retrieve
its recorded version and download it.

01:24:22.282 --> 01:24:26.960
Keep original reports, artifact integrity
evidence and the approved access

01:24:26.960 --> 01:24:28.591
restrictions.

01:24:28.591 --> 01:24:32.770
The incident workspace has separate
awareness clocks and filing-evidence

01:24:32.770 --> 01:24:34.127
forms.

01:24:34.127 --> 01:24:38.877
Follow the actual applicable reporting
procedure and record its real confirmation

01:24:38.877 --> 01:24:40.032
there.

01:24:40.032 --> 01:24:45.496
An exported JSON pack, notification log or
training reference cannot stand in for a

01:24:45.496 --> 01:24:47.912
submission acknowledgement.

01:24:48.642 --> 01:24:52.975
Set the hospital display name and reviewed
colour, and choose whether the public

01:24:52.975 --> 01:24:56.961
preference centre and patient code sign-in
are enabled.

01:24:56.961 --> 01:24:59.068
Check the saved state.

01:24:59.068 --> 01:25:04.365
A custom hostname field does not configure
DNS, TLS or a commissioned branded

01:25:04.365 --> 01:25:05.949
deployment.

01:25:05.949 --> 01:25:10.901
Enable patient code access only after the
verified account and private delivery

01:25:10.901 --> 01:25:13.472
workflows have been accepted.

01:25:13.472 --> 01:25:18.399
Keep the hospital’s privacy contact and
patient support route clear.

01:25:19.100 --> 01:25:24.669
The patient code route is for an existing
independently verified patient account.

01:25:24.669 --> 01:25:29.800
Enter the correct hospital, hospital
number and authorised private channel.

01:25:29.800 --> 01:25:34.597
A generic acknowledgement does not create
an account or confirm that a submitted

01:25:34.597 --> 01:25:37.133
number belongs to a patient.

01:25:37.133 --> 01:25:42.133
The code is private sign-in material and
must never be shared with reception.

01:25:42.133 --> 01:25:46.990
Required account verification and
authenticator checks still apply.

01:25:46.990 --> 01:25:52.745
For enrolment or recovery, use the
hospital’s separate verified procedure.

01:25:53.475 --> 01:25:59.332
An authorised administrator configures the
approved identity provider using its HTTPS

01:25:59.332 --> 01:26:05.022
issuer, registered client identifier,
public pinned RSA key, authorization and

01:26:05.022 --> 01:26:08.746
token endpoints, and exact callback URI.

01:26:08.746 --> 01:26:13.163
The endpoints must follow the configured
issuer restrictions.

01:26:13.163 --> 01:26:16.925
Never paste a private signing key or
password here.

01:26:16.925 --> 01:26:20.877
Changes require current authentication and
evidence.

01:26:20.877 --> 01:26:25.520
This recording shows the configuration
form without commissioning a real provider

01:26:25.520 --> 01:26:29.207
or fabricating a successful external
sign-in.

01:26:29.933 --> 01:26:34.290
Staff single sign-on starts with the
selected hospital and its configured

01:26:34.290 --> 01:26:36.490
identity provider.

01:26:36.490 --> 01:26:40.871
The browser returns through the approved
callback; the application validates the

01:26:40.871 --> 01:26:45.585
protected sign-in flow and any required
authenticator step.

01:26:45.585 --> 01:26:50.894
Staff accounts and roles must already
exist through the approved lifecycle.

01:26:50.894 --> 01:26:55.109
Single sign-on does not create privilege
automatically.

01:26:55.109 --> 01:26:59.811
Synthetic contract or broker assertions
are not evidence of a live SAML or

01:26:59.811 --> 01:27:02.593
hospital provider integration.

01:27:03.308 --> 01:27:07.855
An authorised administrator selects
another current active staff account,

01:27:07.855 --> 01:27:12.105
independently verifies the person under
the hospital procedure and records

01:27:12.105 --> 01:27:14.710
controlled recovery evidence.

01:27:14.710 --> 01:27:18.353
The current record revision and
administrator’s authenticator are

01:27:18.353 --> 01:27:19.793
required.

01:27:19.793 --> 01:27:25.460
Recovery invalidates existing sessions and
requires factor enrolment again.

01:27:25.460 --> 01:27:28.865
This is a powerful identity-root
operation.

01:27:28.865 --> 01:27:33.817
Reauthentication and a saved attestation
are not independent dual approval or proof

01:27:33.817 --> 01:27:36.996
that identity checking actually occurred.

01:27:36.996 --> 01:27:41.633
Keep the hospital’s broader
privileged-access controls in force.

01:27:42.350 --> 01:27:47.671
Create a recognisable course title, target
staff role and version, then inspect the

01:27:47.671 --> 01:27:49.752
enrolment records.

01:27:49.752 --> 01:27:54.502
Versions make it possible to distinguish
old and current material.

01:27:54.502 --> 01:27:58.966
The application is a basic assignment and
completion tracker; it is not an

01:27:58.966 --> 01:28:02.430
independently graded learning-management
system.

01:28:02.430 --> 01:28:07.311
Assign this detailed course to appropriate
staff and keep role-specific practice,

01:28:07.311 --> 01:28:11.962
assessment and support routes available
before operational use.

01:28:12.683 --> 01:28:17.373
A staff member selects their own assigned
enrolment and records the actual passing

01:28:17.373 --> 01:28:21.525
assessment result only after completing
the assessment.

01:28:21.525 --> 01:28:27.228
The visible score range does not create a
test or establish learning by itself.

01:28:27.228 --> 01:28:31.287
Our recording shows the form without
claiming that a human completed an

01:28:31.287 --> 01:28:32.811
assessment.

01:28:32.811 --> 01:28:37.454
Retain the underlying assessment evidence
through the hospital procedure.

01:28:37.454 --> 01:28:42.775
Do not tick the attestation simply to make
the training dashboard look complete.

01:28:43.517 --> 01:28:48.040
Open the supplied regulatory item and
review the official source outside this

01:28:48.040 --> 01:28:49.883
offline capture.

01:28:49.883 --> 01:28:54.764
Confirm its current applicability with the
accountable legal or privacy owner, then

01:28:54.764 --> 01:28:58.943
retain the review date and decision in the
hospital register.

01:28:58.943 --> 01:29:03.859
The supplied list is curated; it is not a
live legal-monitoring feed or automatic

01:29:03.859 --> 01:29:06.097
interpretation service.

01:29:06.097 --> 01:29:11.181
A reviewed label records an action, not a
guarantee that every hospital duty has

01:29:11.181 --> 01:29:13.777
been identified or met.

01:29:14.517 --> 01:29:18.933
Run the due-review job and inspect its
returned result and created work-list

01:29:18.933 --> 01:29:20.383
entries.

01:29:20.383 --> 01:29:24.252
Assign owners and check the actual review
records.

01:29:24.252 --> 01:29:29.788
Entry creation does not prove an email,
SMS or other notification was delivered,

01:29:29.788 --> 01:29:33.443
and it does not complete the underlying
obligation.

01:29:33.443 --> 01:29:38.121
Qualify scheduling, alert delivery,
escalation and operational ownership

01:29:38.121 --> 01:29:41.202
separately in the intended deployment.

01:29:41.933 --> 01:29:46.133
Review the reported field-encryption mode
and cutover state.

01:29:46.133 --> 01:29:50.633
Protected field sidecars are not proof
that every operational name or phone

01:29:50.633 --> 01:29:56.013
column, backup, exported report or
connected system is encrypted.

01:29:56.013 --> 01:30:01.061
Key custody, rotation, restoration,
deployment configuration and independent

01:30:01.061 --> 01:30:05.156
security assessment need their own
operational evidence.

01:30:05.156 --> 01:30:10.525
